INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(181275,'zero point genesis|the pretty wild|the pretty wild|lp','Zero.Point.Genesis','The Pretty Wild','The Pretty Wild','LP','SUMR3594.1','198704654343',18.25,18.25,'45534645','2026-11-10 23:54:58','2026-11-10 23:54:58','/19870465434','(Colored Vinyl, Black, Purple, White)',0,'Debut album from The Pretty Wild, the Las Vegas duo of sisters Jules and Jyl whom weave elements of Metalcore, Pop, Electronic and more into an undefinable, unforgettable debut album project. Black in Purple Color in Color w/ White Splatter Colored Vinyl','11/21/2025',0.7099999999999999645,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/75/4458575-3450924.jpg?ae=4621895153','Heavy Metal');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(181276,'bern rsd|roy hargrove|roy hargrove|lp','Bern (RSD)','Roy Hargrove','Roy Hargrove','LP','TETV30.1','198704749346',28.0,28.0,'45949722','2026-11-10 23:54:58','2026-11-10 23:54:58','/19870474934','(RSD Exclusive, Limited Edition)',0,'"For the first time ever, Roy Hargrove''s legendary 2000 performance at the Bern Jazz Festival is officially released-restored from the original tapes and remastered for audiophile fidelity. This is Hargrove at the height of his powers: bold, lyrical, endlessly inventive. Fronting a stellar quintet of Larry Willis, Sherman Irby, Gerald Cannon, and Willie Jones, he bridges bebop tradition with 21st-century soul, moving effortlessly between hard-swinging post-bop, Latin-inflected grooves, and breathtaking ballads. Long regarded as a highlight by those lucky enough to be in the room, this release captures that lightning for the world. Roy Hargrove''s contributions to jazz were vast, bridging classic form and modern expression like few of his generation. This long-lost performance is both a celebration and a rediscovery-an essential document of one of jazz''s true voices, now heard in full brilliance for the first time. Transferred from the original tapes and restored and mastered by Matthew Lutthans at The Mastering Lab. The limited-edition 180-gram 1-LP edition includes an extensive booklet with rare photographs, newly commissioned liner notes, and testimonials from band members and those influenced by his work." RSD 2026 Exclusive Limited Edition 180g LP with Booklet','4/18/2026',0.7299999999999999823,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/00/4489600-3519075.jpg?ae=4621895153','Jazz');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(181277,'at the earl of old town|terry callier|terry callier|lp','At the Earl of Old Town','Terry Callier','Terry Callier','LP','TETV40.1','198704749285',32.54999999999999715,32.54999999999999715,'45949746','2026-11-10 23:54:58','2026-11-10 23:54:58','/19870474928','(Limited Edition)',0,'For the first time ever, experience Terry Callier as few ever did: live, raw, and on the brink of greatness. Captured in 1967 - predating the release of his cult-classic debut The New Folk Sound of Terry Callier - this intimate, previously unreleased live performance reveals a young artist already operating in his own universe. These 1967 live tapes-unearthed from a private archive were recorded by Joe Segal in Chicago at The Earl of Old Town Club in 1967. Showcasing Callier''s distinctive blend of folk, soul, and jazz in it''s purest form. His intricate guitar work, luminous voice, and spiritual depth are presented in stunning clarity, giving both longtime fans and new listeners an unfiltered glimpse into a foundational moment in American music history. Transferred from the original tapes, restored by Joe Lizzi and mastered by Matthew Lutthans at The Mastering Lab. The limited-edition 180-gram 2-LP edition includes a booklet with rare photographs and newly commissioned liner notes. Also available on CD & Digital. Limited Edition 180g 2xLP Set with Booklet','4/24/2026',1.129999999999999893,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/02/4489602-3519074.jpg?ae=4621895153','Folk');
