INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(181281,'love dance|woody shaw|woody shaw|lp','Love Dance','Woody Shaw','Woody Shaw','LP','TETV4.1','198704749261',28.0,28.0,'45706967','2026-11-10 23:54:58','2026-11-10 23:54:58','/19870474926','(180 Gram Vinyl, Remastered)',0,'Remastered, 180g Vinyl. Including an insert with newly written liner notes by Bob Blumenthal and Barney Fields with rare photograph by K. Abe. Originally released in 1976 on Muse Records, ''Love Dance'' stands as one of Woody Shaw''s most spiritual and forward-thinking sessions. This audiophile reissue restores the album''s full tonal richness, capturing Shaw''s soaring trumpet lines and the ensemble''s dynamic interplay with unprecedented clarity. Shaw leads a powerhouse lineup - including Billy Harper, Steve Turre, Ren├⌐ McLean, Cecil McBee and Joe Bonner - through five expansive tracks blending modal jazz, spiritual themes, and post-bop intensity. A landmark in Shaw''s discography, ''Love Dance'' is essential listening - now presented with the depth and detail it has always deserved. Remastered & Cut AAA directly from the original analog tapes by Matthew Lutthans at The Mastering Lab. Pressed on 180g vinyl at Optimal Media and housed in Stoughton Old Style┬« Tip-On Jackets. Including an insert with newly written liner notes by Bob Blumenthal and Barney Fields with rare photograph by K. Abe.','1/30/2026',0.8499999999999999778,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/74/4472374-3477848.jpg?ae=4621895153','Jazz');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(181282,'leather temple|carpenter brut|carpenter brut|lp','Leather Temple','Carpenter Brut','Carpenter Brut','LP','NOQU0478451.1','198704784514',19.85000000000000143,19.85000000000000143,'45805578','2026-11-10 23:54:58','2026-11-10 23:54:58','/19870478451','(Gatefold LP Jacket)',0,'Across ten tracks, Leather Temple, the third and final chapter of the Leather trilogy channels a raw and nervous energy, somewhere between saturated electro, industrial fever, and 90s synthetic pulse. Yet behind this intensity also lies a cinematic and orchestral dimension, with arrangements that expand the horizon and add dramatic scope. A tight format, a constant intensity: Leather Temple goes all in on impact, balancing raw immediacy with the feel of a post-apocalyptic movie soundtrack. Black Vinyl in Gatefold Jacket','2/27/2026',0.9200000000000000399,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/93/4479593-3502038.jpg?ae=4621895153','Electronic');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(181283,'leather temple|carpenter brut|carpenter brut|lp','Leather Temple','Carpenter Brut','Carpenter Brut','LP','NOQU478452.1','198704784521',19.85000000000000143,19.85000000000000143,'45805585','2026-11-10 23:54:58','2026-11-10 23:54:58','/19870478452','(Colored Vinyl, Yellow, Gatefold LP Jacket)',0,'Across ten tracks, Leather Temple, the third and final chapter of the Leather trilogy channels a raw and nervous energy, somewhere between saturated electro, industrial fever, and 90s synthetic pulse. Yet behind this intensity also lies a cinematic and orchestral dimension, with arrangements that expand the horizon and add dramatic scope. A tight format, a constant intensity: Leather Temple goes all in on impact, balancing raw immediacy with the feel of a post-apocalyptic movie soundtrack. Indie/Retail Exclusive Yellow Colored Vinyl in Gatefold Jacket','2/27/2026',0.910000000000000031,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/94/4479594-3513192.jpg?ae=4621895153','Electronic');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(181284,'double exposure|joe chambers|joe chambers|lp','Double Exposure','Joe Chambers','Joe Chambers','LP','TETV5.1','198704749254',28.0,28.0,'45706974','2026-11-10 23:54:58','2026-11-10 23:54:58','/19870474925',NULL,0,'Originally released in 1978 on Muse Records, Double Exposure is a rare and genre-blurring session that brings together two visionary musicians in a highly personal, exploratory setting. Drummer-composer Joe Chambers-best known for his work with Wayne Shorter, Bobby Hutcherson, and Freddie Hubbard-is joined by Larry Young, a pioneering jazz organist whose modal and avant-garde leanings helped define Tony Williams'' Lifetime and Miles Davis''s Bitches Brew era. Remastered & Cut AAA directly from the original analog tapes by Matthew Lutthans at The Mastering Lab. Pressed on 180g vinyl at Optimal Media and housed in Stoughton Old Style┬« Tip-On Jackets. Including an insert with newly written liner notes by Bill Milkowski and Barney Fields with rare photographs by Jan Persson and Raymond Ross.','1/30/2026',0.8599999999999999867,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/75/4472375-3477847.jpg?ae=4621895153','Jazz');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(181285,'trying times|james blake|james blake|cd','Trying Times [Explicit Content]','James Blake','James Blake','CD','GDBY8704834.2','198704834653',9.75,9.75,'45949609','2026-11-10 23:54:58','2026-11-10 23:54:58','/19870483465','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'English producer, songwriter, and musician James Blake returns with ''Trying Times'', his seventh studio album and first fully independent release. Written between London and Los Angeles, the album confronts the turbulence of the last several years - global unrest, fractured discourse, and personal reckonings while searching for empathy, connection, and love amid chaos. Available on 2 LP Gatefold Vinyl and CD.','3/13/2026',0.2000000000000000111,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/88/4489588-3519486.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
