INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(181875,'greatest|duran duran|duran duran|lp','Greatest','Duran Duran','Duran Duran','LP','RPLH283047.1','5021732830470',27.64000000000000056,27.64000000000000056,'45806834','2026-11-10 23:55:34','2026-11-10 23:55:34','/502173283047',NULL,0,'Duran Duran Greatest, the band''s definitive hits package, is being reissued on black vinyl for the first time since it''s initial release in 1998. Greatest features 19 Duran Duran classics including Rio, Reflex, Ordinary World, Come Undone, Hungry Like The Wolf, Girls on Film and many more.','1/30/2026',1.149999999999999911,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/17/4447217-3520830.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(181876,'movement|new order|new order|lp','Movement','New Order','New Order','LP','RHI836359.1','5021732836359',22.07000000000000028,22.07000000000000028,'45475627','2026-11-10 23:55:34','2026-11-10 23:55:34','/502173283635','(Remastered)',0,'Featuring remastered audio from 2019 previously only available in the ''Movement Definitive Edition'' boxsetThe debut album from New Order, originally produced by Martin Hannett, who had previously collaborated with Joy Division, features eight original tracks all written after the sudden death of Joy Division''s Ian Curtis, including ''Dreams Never End'' and ''Truth'' which were both penned very shortly in a writing session in the summer of 1980. The album charted at #1 spot on the UK independent albums chart in 1981.','10/31/2025',0.5300000000000000266,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/57/4453957-3471218.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(181877,'portal|balu brigada|balu brigada|lp','Portal','Balu Brigada','Balu Brigada','LP','ATL283161.1','5021732831613',22.07000000000000028,22.07000000000000028,'45739293','2026-11-10 23:55:34','2026-11-10 23:55:34','/502173283161','(180 Gram Vinyl)',0,'Portal is the debut full-length album from Balu Brigada, the genre-blurring groove-pop duo made up of New Zealand brothers Henry and Pierre Beasely. Written, produced, and recorded entirely by the pair over three years in cities across the globe - from New York to Berlin to Auckland - the album captures a wide emotional and sonic spectrum, balancing experimental alt-pop with festival-ready hooks. Built on lush instrumentation, slippery basslines, and layered synths, Portal explores themes of escapism, vulnerability, and self-discovery, while reflecting the duo''s deep creative bond and hands-on approach. The result is a bold, cathartic, and immersive debut that marks a major step forward for a band known for pushing the boundaries of modern pop','1/2/2026',0.6099999999999999867,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/62/4475262-3527053.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
