INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(182095,'halo original trilogy original soundtrack|o donnell martin salvatori michael|o donnell martin salvatori michael|lp','Halo Original Trilogy (Original Soundtrack)','O''DONNELL,MARTIN / SALVATORI,MICHAEL','O''DONNELL,MARTIN / SALVATORI,MICHAEL','LP','LCD235.1','5063176042316',126.0,126.0,'44797911','2026-11-10 23:55:47','2026-11-10 23:55:47','/506317604231','(Boxed Set, Remastered)',0,'Halo Studios and Laced Records have teamed up to bring the iconic music of the original Halo trilogy to vinyl for the first time. This box set features 83 tracks from the first three Halo titles, specially remastered for vinyl and pressed onto eight heavyweight LPs. Each game soundtrack will be housed in a wide-spined outer sleeve with printed inner sleeves.','4/2/2027',6.049999999999999823,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/62/4389862-3296208.jpg?ae=4621895153','Soundtrack,Video Game Soundtrack');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(182096,'the kiss of morning iex|graham coxon|graham coxon|lp','The Kiss Of Morning (IEX) [Explicit Content]','Graham Coxon','Graham Coxon','LP','TGIV9241XX.1','5063176118813',27.28999999999999915,27.28999999999999915,'46455536','2026-11-10 23:55:47','2026-11-10 23:55:47','/506317611881','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics, Indie Exclusive, Colored Vinyl, Turquoise)',0,'Arriving in 2002, Graham Coxon''s fourth solo album presented an audible stepping up of both the guitarist''s songwriting and arranging skills. ''Baby You''re out of My Mind''s deft fingerpicking nodded to early Bob Dylan, ''Locked Doors'' grooved along a loose R&B boogie, while ''It Ain''t No Lie''s pared-back riffs were cut from a similar cloth to then newly emerging duo The White Stripes. Less of a DIY affair than it''s predecessors the album features pedal steel player B.J. Cole and Louis Vause on keyboards, whhelped to fully flesh out the eclectic fare on offer. "I felt free to do whatever I wanted to do. I was expanding my sound and also finding a bit more calm in my songs" says Graham. ΓÇï"operates on a level of perversity, honesty and originality that blows most bands out of the water" - NME. Available as part of a comprehensive catalogue campaign via Transgressive. Faithfully reproduced packaging: kraftboard outer sleeve with silver foiling. Includes 12-page booklet of photos and credits. Follows his first wave of reissues in June, which included the critically acclaimed unreleased studio album Castle Park (reached #6 on the OCC Independent Chart). 5-date UK tour in November including SOLD OUT Kentish Town Forum','9/11/2026',1.209999999999999965,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/81/4530281-3673220.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(182097,'tough town|bryan adams|bryan adams|lp','Tough Town','Bryan Adams','Bryan Adams','LP','BADC610511.1','5063176105110',23.51999999999999958,23.51999999999999958,'45978449','2026-11-10 23:55:47','2026-11-10 23:55:47','/506317610511','(RSD Exclusive, Booklet)',0,'STOCK DEPLETED. This compilation features previously unreleased tracks and non-album material, including the song "Tough Town" itself. Never been released on vinyl previously only available as part of a deluxe box set on CD - includes photo booklet.','4/18/2026',0.5699999999999999512,'lb','https://webami.aent.com/content/img/no_image_CD_lrg.gif','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(182098,'dune awakening original soundtrack|knut avenstroup haugen|knut avenstroup haugen|lp','Dune: Awakening (Original Soundtrack)','Knut Avenstroup Haugen','Knut Avenstroup Haugen','LP','LAC301.1','5063176088819',30.0,30.0,'45464294','2026-11-10 23:55:47','2026-11-10 23:55:47','/506317608881','(180 Gram Vinyl)',0,'Bless the Maker: the Great Houses of Laced Records and Funcom have forged a temporary trade agreement to bring you the expansive soundtrack for Dune: Awakening on vinyl. The hit survival game has garnered critical praise for it''s incredibly faithful and detailed realisation of the Dune universe-from it''s sprawling vistas to deep lore and political intrigue. The music is integral in recreating the atmosphere of Arrakis, conjuring not only it''s striking landscapes but the human experience of life on the planet. Recorded live at Air Studios in London with The Chamber Orchestra of London, Haugen''s soundtrack conjures a planetary sense of scale. Arcing strings shimmer and twist weightless in the air like heat rising from the desert floor, while resonant brass evokes dawn stretching out across the sands. The luscious acoustic instrumentation is enhanced and elevated by rippling electronics, capturing Dune''s singular blend of science fiction and spiritual tradition. Soaring vocal performances from Clara Sorace, Eurielle and Em├¡lia Rovira Alegre centre this sense of the sacred, pushing the soundtrack to ecstatic emotional peaks.','2/13/2026',1.129999999999999893,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/86/4452986-3450754.jpg?ae=4621895153','Soundtrack,Video Game Soundtrack');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(182099,'crow sit on blood tree iex|graham coxon|graham coxon|lp','Crow Sit On Blood Tree (IEX) [Explicit Content]','Graham Coxon','Graham Coxon','LP','TGIV9331XX.1','5063176118516',25.98999999999999844,25.98999999999999844,'46455550','2026-11-10 23:55:47','2026-11-10 23:55:47','/506317611851','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics, Indie Exclusive, Colored Vinyl, Red, Black)',0,'Originally released in 2001, Graham''s third solo album, Crow Sit On Blood Tree, found him stretching his wings as a songwriter. While the likes of ''Burn It Down'' and ''You Will Never Be'' buzzed with the same noisy alt-rock energy he''d brought to bear on iconic Blur tracks such as ''Song 2'', on the record''s gentler moments, such as ''All Has Gone'' and ''Thank God For The Rain'', he showed he could also master the delicate acoustic folk of Nick Drake and Bert Jansch. "There''s absolute mayhem on that at times, but there''s quiet songs, too," Graham says of the record, which was recorded, mixed and mastered in just two weeks. "I was still exploring different music and what I could do. I''ll turn my hand to so many different types of music if it feels natural." Available again as part of a comprehensive reissue of Coxon''s solo catalogue on Transgressive. Follows his first wave of reissues in June, which included the critically acclaimed unreleased studio album Castle Park (reached #6 on the OCC Independent Chart). 5-date UK tour in November including SOLD OUT Kentish Town Forum','9/11/2026',0.9000000000000000222,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/83/4530283-3673217.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(182100,'13 yellow|white denim|white denim|lp','13 - Yellow','White Denim','White Denim','LP','BAUI1687.1','5065019688972',23.37999999999999901,23.37999999999999901,'45945571','2026-11-10 23:55:47','2026-11-10 23:55:47','/506501968897','(Colored Vinyl, Yellow, 140 Gram Vinyl)',0,'13, the thirteenth album of White Denim''s career, is an incandescent, groove-heavy alchemy of rock, funk, dub, soul and down-dirty blues - and plenty more besides - it''s imbued with the same questing spirit that''s been the band''s trademark since first starting in Austin, Texas, some 20 years ago. Petralli''s wide-ranging musical appetites have become more voracious over time. The sounds and textures of ''13'' are informed by everyone from Scritti Politti to The Gap Band, Terry Reid to King Tubby, Caetano Veloso to John Cale, Stevie Wonder to ''80s-era Steve Winwood. Such diversity is refl ected in multi-faceted gems like "(God Created) Lock And Key", "Only A Fool" and "That''s Rap". For Fans Of: Ty Segall, King Gizzard & The Wizard Lizard, Grateful Dead','4/24/2026',0.5200000000000000177,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/30/4489230-3518395.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(182101,'goodbye small head sea blue|ezra furman|ezra furman|lp','Goodbye Small Head - Sea Blue','Ezra Furman','Ezra Furman','LP','BAUI1646.1','5065019688750',20.78999999999999915,20.78999999999999915,'44989149','2026-11-10 23:55:47','2026-11-10 23:55:47','/506501968875','(Colored Vinyl, Blue)',0,'Goodbye Small Head is the name of the new record from Ezra Furman. Twelve songs, twelve variations on the experience of completely losing control, whether by weakness, illness, mysticism, BDSM, drugs, heartbreak or just living in a sick society with one''s eyes open. These songs are vivid with overwhelm. They''re not about someone going off the rails, they are inside that person''s heart. The songwriting here is a revision to William Wordsworth''s famous proclamation that "Poetry is the spontaneous overflow of powerful feelings: it takes it''s origin from emotion recollected in tranquility." This poetry, my poetry, arrived in the midst of the storm. It was written as I teetered toward the edge. The band and I had had a run of records that were very communal, very first person plural. We, us, ours. I was trying to exist in and create a shared space with my audience, make anthems for taking care of one another in dark times. But there does come a time when a woman is left alone in a room to unravel. And you need anthems for those times too. GSH also reflects a band reaching a new peak of our powers. If I were a music journalist, I would call this an orchestral emo prog-rock record sprinkled with samples. Thank goodness I''m not a music journalist! I think of this music as cinematic and intense. A friend of mine said it sounded like "the coolest movie soundtrack of 1997," and I''m quite pleased with that description. We''ve incorporated a small string section into eight of the twelve tracks, and are using samples for the first time-nothing you''d recognize, just some uncredited singing that Sam found online, chopped into beautifully evocative bits. Other than that, this record features something that''s become nearly an anachronism: a band that''s been playing real instruments together for over a decade, intuitively in touch with each other as musicians. Four players in a room together who know exactly how to respond to one another. We recorded in Chicago with Brian Deck producing; a return to both my city of origin and my producer of origin, since Deck produced my first rock''n''roll records many years ago (Banging Down the Doors (2007) and Inside the Human Body (2008) by Ezra Furman & the Harpoons). In some way I think I was trying to return to some much younger mindset, when all the intensity and fear and emotion of life was less mediated by adult coping mechanisms. When it was all brand new with no filter. Though I wrote parts of it earlier, I think the making of this album really began on the morning of April 11th 2023, when I woke suddenly ill, limped into the bathroom and lost consciousness. At the hospital they gave me all the tests and told me that actually, I wasn''t sick, and I could go home now. I stayed in bed for months, exhausted and in pain, no doctor offering any convincing explanation or cure. After a while I began hemorrhaging songs. Many of these songs arrived unexpectedly and left my body violently. All of them seemed to be steeped in the helpless transcendence of being suddenly overcome, undone. The lyrics to album opener "Grand Mal" and it''s following companion "Sudden Storm" were written in one hypomanic sitting after talking to an epileptic friend about the mystical quality of certain major seizures. "Jump Out" is a panicked rocker for realizing you are going to have to leap from a moving vehicle because the driver has no intention of letting you out. "Power of the Moon" is an existentialist wrestling match with whoever''s in charge of the universe, and "Submission" is the combination of dread and relief felt when you realize the long-suffering "good guys" have no chance against 21st-century forces of evil. And that''s just Side A. Is it dark? Yeah! Is it also wonder-struck, laced with psychedelic beauty, triumphant in it''s wounded way? Yeah again. 140g sea blue LP, 2 pg insert','5/16/2025',0.5699999999999999512,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/40/4408740-3329451.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
