INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(182334,'rain dogs|tom waits|tom waits|lp','Rain Dogs','Tom Waits','Tom Waits','LP','ISLB003707801.1','602448898531',23.25,23.25,'43657117','2026-11-10 23:56:00','2026-11-10 23:56:00','/60244889853','(180 Gram Vinyl)',0,'Noted as Tom WaitsΓÇÖ most critically acclaimed album, Rain Dogs follows the new musical path Waits had taken with Swordfishtrombones. Considered the middle of a de facto trilogy with Swordfishtrombones and Franks Wild Years, Rain Dogs is the first of WaitsΓÇÖ albums to be written in New York, in a Lower Manhattan basement. A 53-minute, 19-track monster, Rain Dogs is a kind of mutant, late 20th century musical ΓÇ£Canterbury TalesΓÇ¥ with a shape-shifting band. There are banjos and marimbas and bowed saw and parade drum and howling horns (and Keith Richards and Marc Ribot) on this rollicking, rough-hewn opusΓÇöand Waits, using his voice in increasingly weird-and-wild ways. The songs are stories, sagas, laments, breakdowns, character studies, comedies and cabaret numbers. ThereΓÇÖs the aching ΓÇ£Hang Down Your Head,ΓÇ¥ and the moving anthem, ΓÇ£Downtown Train,ΓÇ¥ which was covered by Patti Smith and Rod Stewart. Waits coined the term, ΓÇ£rain dog,ΓÇ¥ a reference to dogs who lose their way when touchstone scents are washed away in storms. Among the lost dogs on the album: gruff, wandering merchant marines (ΓÇ£SingaporeΓÇ¥), an accordion player in a slaughterhouse (ΓÇ£Cemetery PolkaΓÇ¥), a ΓÇ£jockey full of bourbonΓÇ¥ (also the song title), an abandoned, withdrawn woman (ΓÇ£TimeΓÇ¥), a ΓÇ£gun street girl,ΓÇ¥ the old drunks and hustlers of Union Square, and even Waits, himself: Aboard a shipwreck train / Give my umbrella to the Rain Dogs / For I am a Rain Dog, too. . . Originally released in 1985 on Island Records, the album is newly remastered for the first time ever from the original ┬╜ΓÇ¥ flat master tape and personally overseen by Tom Waits and Kathleen Brennan. Mastered by Chris Bellman at Bernie Grundman Mastering under the guidance of WaitsΓÇÖ longtime audio engineer, Karl Derfler. The album packaging has also been restored. Rain Dogs includes tracks such as ΓÇ£Downtown Train,ΓÇ¥ ΓÇ£Clap HandsΓÇ¥ and ΓÇ£Jockey Full Of Bourbon.ΓÇ¥ Available on 180g black vinyl. Tom Waits ΓÇö "Rain Dogs"','9/22/2023',0.3900000000000000133,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/42/4232942-3021521.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(182335,'just because bone colored vinyl import|claire rosinkranz|claire rosinkranz|lp','Just Because - Bone Colored Vinyl [Import]','Claire Rosinkranz','Claire Rosinkranz','LP','EMDI5517893.1','602455178930',29.08999999999999986,29.08999999999999986,'43428625','2026-11-10 23:56:00','2026-11-10 23:56:00','/60245517893','(Colored Vinyl, White, United Kingdom - Import)',0,'Limited white colored vinyl LP pressing. On ''Just Because'', Claire captures all of the joy, confusion, anxiety, and wonder of growing up through 13 tracks set to a soundtrack of gleeful guitars, lo-fi production, and chantable choruses-all under the California sun. Throughout 2022, she wrote and recorded the album with producers Afterhrs, Paul Phamous, Stint, Elie Rizk, and her most frequent collaborator, executive producer, and dad Ragnar Rosinkranz. On the album, she states, ''Just Because is a collection of songs I wrote about my life as an 18 year old. It''s a window into my world as I''m growing up and navigating life. Enjoy stepping into my lil movie.'' Over a soundtrack of alternative pop spiked with just the right amount of punk and electronics, Claire Rosinkranz asserts herself as a true Gen-Z storyteller whose vision instantly captivates.','10/13/2023',0.5,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/40/4200340-3413707.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(182336,'swordfishtrombones|tom waits|tom waits|lp','Swordfishtrombones','Tom Waits','Tom Waits','LP','ISLB003707401.1','602448898425',23.25,23.25,'43657124','2026-11-10 23:56:00','2026-11-10 23:56:00','/60244889842','(180 Gram Vinyl)',0,'2023 Marks forty years since Tom Waits released Swordfishtrombones, ushering in a new and critically acclaimed musical era for Waits and his longtime songwriting and production partner, Brennan. Waits went from ΓÇÿ70ΓÇÖs-era ΓÇ£bluesy, boozyΓÇ¥ wordsmith and melodist with seven albums behind him to sound sculptor, miner of the subconscious, abstract orchestrator, sonic cubistΓÇöwhile retaining his innate lyricism, melodic invention, humanity. As he put it in a 1983 interview: ΓÇ£I tried to listen to the noise in my head and invent some junkyard orchestral deviationΓÇöa mutant apparatus to drive this noise into a wreck collection.ΓÇ¥ ItΓÇÖs a Waits-arranged pastiche, a variety of atmospheres from different sound planets. There is the warped, marching-army-ants music of ΓÇ£Underground,ΓÇ¥ an impressionist chant about people living below cities, but there was also the poignancy of the spare piano ballad, ΓÇ£SoldierΓÇÖs Things,ΓÇ¥ the good bar yarn, ΓÇ£FrankΓÇÖs Wild YearsΓÇ¥, the tender, minimalist paean to WaitsΓÇÖ wife and muse, Kathleen, ΓÇ£Johnsburg, Illinois,ΓÇ¥ and the raggedy anthem to neighborhood chaos, ΓÇ£In the Neighborhood.ΓÇ¥ ΓÇ£On Swordfishtrombones, Waits has made a breakthrough ΓÇô heΓÇÖs found music as evocative as his words. WaitsΓÇÖs grumble of a voice now bounces off a peculiar assortment of horns and percussion and organ and keyboards, as if heΓÇÖd led a Salvation Army band into a broken-down Hong Kong disco. ItΓÇÖs as if heΓÇÖs shifted from monologues to screenplaysΓÇªΓÇ¥ - Jon Parales January 1984 - GQ Magazine The album is newly remastered for the first time ever from the original EQΓÇÖed ┬╜ΓÇ¥ production master tape and personally overseen by Tom Waits and Kathleen Brennan. Mastered by Chris Bellman at Bernie Grundman Mastering under the guidance of WaitsΓÇÖ longtime audio engineer, Karl Derfler. The album packaging has also been restored. Available on 180g black vinyl. Tom Waits ΓÇö "Swordfishtrombones"','9/22/2023',0.6099999999999999867,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/40/4232940-3021536.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(182337,'the chronic|dr dre|dr dre|lp','The Chronic [Explicit Content]','Dr Dre','Dr Dre','LP','ISCB003760301.1','602455099969',31.16000000000000014,31.16000000000000014,'43311224','2026-11-10 23:56:00','2026-11-10 23:56:00','/60245509996','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'Double vinyl LP pressing. The Chronic is the debut studio album by the hip hop producer and rapper Dr. Dre, originally released in 1992. The Chronic was Dr. Dre''s first solo album after he departed the hip hop group N.W.A. It features many appearances by then-emerging American rapper Snoop Dogg, who used the album as a launch pad for his own solo career.','4/21/2023',0.930000000000000048,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/49/4182949-2945829.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rap/Hip Hop');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(182338,'messy|olivia dean|olivia dean|lp','Messy','Olivia Dean','Olivia Dean','LP','ISL144000.1','602455215895',27.69000000000000127,27.69000000000000127,'44135324','2026-11-10 23:56:01','2026-11-10 23:56:01','/60245521589',NULL,0,'Vinyl LP pressing. UK soul-pop star Olivia Dean''s long-awaited debut album ''Messy''. Featuring the singles ''Danger'' and ''UFO'', ''Messy'' cements Dean as one of the most original and versatile voices in UK pop. Crafting classic yet conversational hooks with genre-fluid tinges, she''s honed a way of exploring universal themes of love, loss and everything in between with razor-sharp but open-hearted storytelling.','2/23/2024',0.589999999999999969,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/10/4211810-3124713.jpg?ae=4621895153','Vocal');
