INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184070,'mt joy|mt joy|mt joy|cd','Mt. Joy','Mt.Joy','Mt.Joy','CD','DUAT1852.2','803020185227',7.790000000000000035,7.790000000000000035,'35670629','2026-11-10 23:57:35','2026-11-10 23:57:35','/80302018522',NULL,0,'Steeped in folk-rock tradition and powered by the intuitive creative connection between Matt Quinn (vocals, guitar) and Sam Cooper (guitar), the songs on Mt. Joy''s eponymous debut depict the former wrestling with his own conscience, where the mundane and the fantastic collide as he processes tragedy, society, and love. Opener "I''m Your Wreck" describes "monsters in (the) closet, using up the wi-fi" as it cycles from it''s desperate, spiraling verses to it''s swinging, stubbornly optimistic coda, while the loping, plaintive chords of "Younger Days" meditate on a frayed psyche and the fear of choosing the wrong path. "Sheep," with it''s collapsing, hoarse-voiced cry of "freedom was paid in blood," is a post-Trump salvo on the responsibilities of the fortunate to overcome political and social despondency. "Astrovan" is a warm, yearning bit of road-trip philosophy that posits the existence of a Deadhead Jesus cruising the dusty highways of the countryside. And on "Silver Lining," perhaps the album''s brightest moment, Quinn surveys the damage of hard drugs and the vicious cycle of addiction, as the song''s melancholic sentiment kicks into it''s fervid, defiant chorus, all shout-along vocals and trilling guitars.','3/2/2018',0.08999999999999999667,'lb','https://media.aent-m.com/graphics/items/sdimages/a/500/1/8/7/8/3758781.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184071,'evening machines|gregory alan isakov|gregory alan isakov|lp','Evening Machines','Gregory Alan Isakov','Gregory Alan Isakov','LP','DUAT1883.1','803020188310',16.10000000000000143,16.10000000000000143,'36640133','2026-11-10 23:57:35','2026-11-10 23:57:35','/80302018831',NULL,0,'Vinyl LP pressing. Gregory Alan Isakov''s Dualtone debut, Evening Machines, is poised to take his career to places yet unknown. Recorded at a converted barn studio located on Isakov''s three-acre farm in Boulder County, CO, the 12-track album was self-produced and mixed by Tucker Martine (Neko Case, The Decemberists) and Andrew Berlin (Descendants, Rise Against). Since his 2003 debut, Isakov has self-released three LPs on his independent label, Suitcase Town Music and has toured extensively worldwide with the likes of Iron & Wine, Ani DiFranco, Blind Pilot, Passenger, Josh Ritter, Brandi Carlile, and Nathaniel Rateliff. Since his debut with the Colorado Symphony Orchestra in November 2013 he has also performed with several symphonies including the Seattle Symphony, the Oregon Symphony Orchestra, the National Symphony Orchestra, the Atlanta Symphony, and the Vermont Symphony Orchestra. Isakov also has a significant film/TV history with 50 syncs of songs like "Suitcase Full of Sparks," "Amsterdam," "Time Will Tell," "If I Go" and "Only Ghost."','10/5/2018',0.6400000000000000133,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/95/3567395.jpg?ae=4621895153','Pop');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184072,'iii|the lumineers|the lumineers|lp','Iii [Explicit Content]','The Lumineers','The Lumineers','LP','DUAT1951.1','803020195110',14.78999999999999915,14.78999999999999915,'39092052','2026-11-10 23:57:35','2026-11-10 23:57:35','/80302019511','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'Vinyl LP pressing in gatefold jacket. 2019 release. Two-time Grammy-nominated band The Lumineers are back with their third album, III, a cinematic piece presented as a narrative in three chapters, with each one centering on one main character. III''s concept began while the band was writing in the Catskill mountains, where producer Simone Felice works. Decidedly darker than their previous work in concept, but replete with their trademark expressive vocals and dynamic arrangements, III boldly and expertly goes in an artistic direction not yet traveled by the band. The Lumineers have enjoyed substantial commercial success; their 2012 self-titled debut was certified triple-platinum in 2018, and their sophomore album Cleopatra was certified platinum in the same year after it''s 2016 release. They''ve had multiple #1 hits on the Triple A and Alternative radio charts, and have sold out tours across the world; over 300,000 tickets were sold on 2017''s Cleopatra world tour. The Lumineers have also supported icons and their musical heroes on the road, including Tom Petty and the Heartbreakers and U2''s Joshua Tree tour.','9/13/2019',1.280000000000000026,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/75/3674275-2413463.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184073,'the lumineers 10th anniversary edition|the lumineers|the lumineers|lp','The Lumineers - 10th Anniversary Edition','The Lumineers','The Lumineers','LP','DUAT2382.1','803020238213',18.78999999999999915,18.78999999999999915,'42605805','2026-11-10 23:57:35','2026-11-10 23:57:35','/80302023821',NULL,0,'Double 180gm vinyl LP pressing. Digitally remastered and expanded edition featuring 6 tracks previously unreleased on vinyl, new liner notes, and all-new packaging with exclusive behind the scenes photos. The Lumineers'' breakout debut album captured hearts of fans and critics worldwide in 2012, leading to two Grammy-award nominations and a #2 Billboard chart peak. It features the hit singles "Ho Hey" "Stubborn Love" and "Submarines."','2/3/2023',1.260000000000000008,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/66/4084566-2896023.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184074,'roll the bones x gold black vinyl|shakey graves|shakey graves|lp','Roll The Bones X (Gold & Black Vinyl) [Explicit Content]','Shakey Graves','Shakey Graves','LP','DUAT2168.1','803020216815',18.78999999999999915,18.78999999999999915,'41317860','2026-11-10 23:57:35','2026-11-10 23:57:35','/80302021681','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics, Gold, Black, Gatefold LP Jacket)',0,'Double gold and black colored vinyl LP pressing in gatefold jacket. To celebrate the tenth anniversary of Shakey Graves'' debut album, Dualtone is product to release Roll The Bones X on April 2, as a special double-album presentation in a gorgeous high-quality package with a 20-page photo journal. The first disc contains the original studtio record, previously only available through Bandcamp where it garnered over 100,000 downloads. The second, never-before-hear ''odds & Ends'' disc contains live tracks, demos, B-sides, and more.','4/2/2021',1.560000000000000053,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/57/3925457-2665430.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184075,'good for you|houndmouth|houndmouth|lp','Good For You','Houndmouth','Houndmouth','LP','DUAT2227.1','803020222717',13.08999999999999986,13.08999999999999986,'41847176','2026-11-10 23:57:35','2026-11-10 23:57:35','/80302022271',NULL,0,'Vinyl LP pressing. 2021 release from the Americana trio. Recorded with Brad Cook (Waxahatchee, Hiss Golden Messenger) and mixed by Jon Ashley (The War On Drugs, B.J. Barham), the fourth full-length album from the Indiana-bred, platinum-selling band marks a return to what Houndmouth does best: "shaggy, swinging, big-screen storytelling" (NPR Music) set to a rustic, home-recorded sound.','11/5/2021',0.6899999999999999467,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/54/3990854-2733082.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184076,'shadowglow|flipturn|flipturn|lp','Shadowglow [Explicit Content]','Flipturn','Flipturn','LP','DUAT2484.1','803020248410',21.58999999999999986,21.58999999999999986,'42919865','2026-11-10 23:57:35','2026-11-10 23:57:35','/80302024841','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics, Gatefold LP Jacket)',0,'Double vinyl LP housed in gatefold jacket. 2023 release. In the time since 2015, Flipturn has mushroomed to reaches far beyond the walls of the Fernandina Beach garage they first practiced in. Built up by Dillon Basse (lead vocals/rhythm guitar), Tristan Duncan (lead guitar), Madeline Jarman (bass), Mitch Fountain (synth), and Devon VonBalson (drums), the band is walking proof that the DIY approach is still alive and well in the modern music world. Growing up and maturing as musicians in a way that can only be done by spending years on the road together, Flipturn is primed to usher in the era of their debut full-length album.','3/3/2023',1.199999999999999956,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/83/4125083-3409606.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184077,'appaloosa bones|gregory alan isakov|gregory alan isakov|cd','Appaloosa Bones','Gregory Alan Isakov','Gregory Alan Isakov','CD','STWM2554.2','803020255425',9.5,9.5,'43463510','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302025542',NULL,0,'Gregory Alan Isakov wanted to pare it all back on Appaloosa Bones, the Colorado-based singer''s new album. Arrangement-wise, the impulse to keep things simple was a pendulum swing away from his Grammy-nominated 2018 album, Evening Machines. "I set out to make a record that was really bare bones," Isakov says. "I wanted to go backward a little bit, because Evening Machines was such a deep dive into arrangements. I wanted to have more of a raw experience with this one." Isakov played many of the instruments on Appaloosa Bones himself. He recorded in a studio tucked away in a barn on his property outside of Boulder, Colorado, where he helps grow produce for CSA members, local restaurants, and an area food bank. The resulting album is intimate and hushed, but maybe not as spare as what Isakov initially had in mind. The eleven songs on the album are full of lush vocal harmonies and layers of instrumental textures that blend guitar, banjo, piano, and various other keyboards.','8/18/2023',0.1000000000000000055,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/39/4205039-2971239.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184078,'mt joy anniversary edition|mt joy|mt joy|lp','Mt. Joy (anniversary Edition)','Mt. Joy','Mt. Joy','LP','DUAT2539.1','803020253919',18.78999999999999915,18.78999999999999915,'43695997','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302025391','(Anniversary Edition, Etched)',0,'Etched vinyl. Since it''s initial launch in 2018, Mt. Joy''s self-titled debut album has become a timeless classic in the indie folk-rock genre. Mt. Joy earned platinum and gold certifications, selling over 600k records and amassing over 710M streams globally. "Silver Lining," their chart-topping single, remains a defining anthem on Triple A and Alternative radio. Moreover, their relentless dedication to touring has allowed them to leave a lasting impression on audiences worldwide, headlining major music festivals and playing sold-out shows at renowned venues. And we are thrilled to offer a brand new repressing of their debut album featuring three tracks never before available on vinyl, reimagined album art, and an etched picture disc. This is a must have piece for any Mt. Joy fan or record collector alike.','12/1/2023',1.09000000000000008,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/38/4238038-3080437.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184079,'live at red rocks|mt joy|mt joy|lp','Live At Red Rocks [Explicit Content]','Mt. Joy','Mt. Joy','LP','DUAT2380.1','803020238015',15.99000000000000021,15.99000000000000021,'42482192','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302023801','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'Double vinyl LP pressing. Mt. Joy''s climb into the musical stratosphere owes a great deal to their highly energetic and passionate live performances. They''ve sold out room after room across the country, have toured with arena acts like The Lumineers, among many others, and fans the world over flock to their shows. So when the coronavirus pandemic sidelined the touring industry, Mt. Joy felt the effects in a significant way. Fast forward to May 22, 2021: artists and fans alike are finally emerging, and Mt. Joy steps on the stage at Red Rocks Amphitheater, playing the biggest show on record since live music began to open back up. Live At Red Rocks showcases the band''s spirited performance in front of the sold-out Colorado crowd, and the energy felt from the audience''s thrill of experiencing live music again is unmistakable, even through the air waves.','5/6/2022',1.120000000000000107,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/74/4067274-3409604.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184080,'appaloosa bones brown|gregory alan isakov|gregory alan isakov|lp','Appaloosa Bones - Brown','Gregory Alan Isakov','Gregory Alan Isakov','LP','STWM2554.1','803020255418',17.10000000000000143,17.10000000000000143,'43463503','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302025541','(Colored Vinyl, Brown)',0,'Brown Vinyl. Gregory Alan Isakov wanted to pare it all back on Appaloosa Bones, the Colorado-based singer''s new album. Arrangement-wise, the impulse to keep things simple was a pendulum swing away from his Grammy-nominated 2018 album, Evening Machines. "I set out to make a record that was really bare bones," Isakov says. "I wanted to go backward a little bit, because Evening Machines was such a deep dive into arrangements. I wanted to have more of a raw experience with this one."','8/18/2023',0.6199999999999999956,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/38/4205038-2971991.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184081,'live at the salt shed|mt joy|mt joy|lp','Live at the Salt Shed [Explicit Content]','Mt. Joy','Mt. Joy','LP','DUAT2740.1','803020274013',27.08999999999999986,27.08999999999999986,'44575366','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302027401','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'Live at The Salt Shed was recorded over four sold-out nights at the famed Chicago venue to Celebrate New Year''s 2024. Forming in 2016, Mt. Joy made their mark two years later when their self-titled Mt. Joy (2018) debut album spun off platinum single "Silver Lining," an uplifting power ballad that has eclipsed over 240 million streams across platforms. Their second album, Rearrange Us (2020) drew widespread critical raves, with the title track gaining 92 million Spotify streams since the release. Their third LP, Orange Blood (2022), came out of the pandemic and further cemented them with another #1, "Lemon Tree," at AAA and a 70 date headline tour that sold over 180K tickets. Their latest single, "Highway Queen," released March 8th, 2024 hit #2 on AAA radio and continues to grow as the band brings their newest song to the road for a busy 2024 tour. Upcoming plans for 2024 include new music, live shows, and a world tour including shows at Madison Square Garden in New York City, The Hollywood Bowl in Los Angeles, Roundhouse in London, and more. Over the past seven years, Mt. Joy has amassed over half a billion streams and earned acclaim from critics and fans.','11/8/2024',1.620000000000000106,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/21/4366221-3293268.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184082,'live from wrigley field|the lumineers|the lumineers|lp','Live From Wrigley Field [Explicit Content]','The Lumineers','The Lumineers','LP','DUAT2556.1','803020255616',29.98999999999999844,29.98999999999999844,'44371166','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302025561','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'In September of 2022, with over 40,000 fans in attendance, The Lumineers took fans on a anthemic, foot-stomping journey with the BRIGHTSIDE World Tour, ending their largest worldwide tour to date at Chicago''s historic Wrigley Field. Highlighting career favorite tracks like Ho Hey, Ophelia, and Stubborn Love along with modern favorites A.M Radio, Brightside and more, both their sophisticated songwriting and impressive instrumentation and performance chops were on full display. For the band''s first live album ever, the performance will be pressed on a 3-LP vinyl set. Hear The Lumineers like you''ve never heard them before.','9/27/2024',1.850000000000000088,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/82/4340482-3181831.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184083,'brightside|the lumineers|the lumineers|cassette','Brightside','The Lumineers','The Lumineers','Cassette','DUAT2249.4','803020224940',7.69000000000000039,7.69000000000000039,'42040859','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302022494',NULL,0,'Multi-platinum selling GRAMMY-nominated band The Lumineers are back with their fourth record,  ∩╗┐BRIGHTSIDE∩╗┐, releasing January 14, 2022 on Dualtone. ∩╗┐Coming off the success of their darkly cinematic third record ∩╗┐III∩╗┐, Wesley Schultz and Jeremiah Fraites'' latest work is their most spontaneous and joyous yet, featuring their ever-more-sophisticated songwriting and arranging and production from longtime producer and friend Simone Felice. The lead single and title track "BRIGHTSIDE, " recorded in just one day, sets off the album with an anthemic bang, touching on themes of love and American life and featuring the foot-stomping, arena-filling sound the band has become beloved for worldwide. "... this time it was bare bones, " Schultz expressed. "We started demoing in Jer''s basement and didn''t even touch the computer - we just used my phone to record voice memos on, and that was what we sent to Simone. For me, it was about wanting to have more curiosity in the studio and not have everything all dialed in. It felt like a new path."','1/14/2022',0.1100000000000000005,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/40/4011640-2748107.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184084,'lordy|houndmouth|houndmouth|lp','Lordy [Explicit Content]','Houndmouth','Houndmouth','LP','DUAT26681.1','803020266810',18.80000000000000071,18.80000000000000071,'46199515','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302026681','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'Houndmouth frontman Matt Myers, whose band spent the previous decade blending rock & roll and American roots music into radio staples like the chart-topping, platinum-selling "Sedona," struggled for two years to finish new songs. The end of one relationship, the beginning of another, and the all-consuming feeling of new love left him unable to write-until a visit with Grammy-winning producer Brad Cook, who''d overseen Good For You, restarted his songwriting engines and led to the creation of Lordy. For the making of Lordy, Matt enlisted a small circle of musicians including Iron & Wine''s Sam Beam, MJ Lenderman, Phil Cook, and live touring keyboardist Caleb Hickman. "Everything sounds close, like you''re having a close conversation rather than a surface-level conversation." The result is Houndmouth''s most intimate record yet, delivering an emotional punch that lingers long after the music fades.','7/10/2026',0.5799999999999999601,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/38/4511538-3665087.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184085,'something is working up above my head|shovels rope|shovels rope|lp','Something Is Working Up Above My Head','Shovels & Rope','Shovels & Rope','LP','DUAT2721.1','803020272118',15.99000000000000021,15.99000000000000021,'44403997','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302027211','(Clear Vinyl)',0,'From the inimitable husband and wife folk-punk duo that started a movement, Shovels & Rope''s new studio album ''Something Is Working Up Above My Head'' is a catalog of vulnerable characters with sweet and sordid narratives. "Many times we''ve made records that we loved and then, after figuring out how we''d perform it live, we end up falling in love with the live arrangement because being a 2 piece band, it took some real risk and struggle which led to innovation, which gave it a whole new life. So with this one we just started there and worked backwards. The result encapsulates, more than anything we''ve done before, the sound of our live performance. Resulting in what one might consider by definition, a definitive album."','9/6/2024',0.7399999999999999912,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/87/4344287-3200893.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184086,'burnout days|flipturn|flipturn|lp','Burnout Days [Explicit Content]','Flipturn','Flipturn','LP','DUAT28021.1','803020280212',15.99000000000000021,15.99000000000000021,'44690519','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302028021','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics, Colored Vinyl, Red, Orange)',0,'Sunlight color. Burnout Days, the forthcoming sophomore album finds Flipturn returning as sonic architects, harnessing their impressive knack for hooks, shimmering soundscapes and "nostalgia-inducing lyrical delivery" (Uproxx). But on Burnout Days, Flipturn arrives with more grit, craft and vulnerability than ever before - a clear evolution in the band''s sound, and one that reflects their growth as musicians and individuals. Recorded at Sonic Ranch Studios near El Paso, Texas and produced by Chad Copelin (Wilderado, Sasha Sloan, BRONCHO), Burnout Days is inspired by the band''s journey on the road, as they sort through challenges like self-esteem, codependency, addiction and the twists and turns of day-to-day life in one''s mid-twenties. Together, they uncover the beauty that exists even in times of burnout through a mix of raw, rhythmic moments and sonic experimentation - all with a palpable sense of meticulousness and maturity.','1/24/2025',0.6500000000000000222,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/96/4378196-3518376.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184087,'and the war came ten year anniversary edition|shakey graves|shakey graves|lp','And the War Came: Ten Year Anniversary Edition','Shakey Graves','Shakey Graves','LP','DUAT2791.1','803020279117',21.58999999999999986,21.58999999999999986,'44677633','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302027911','(Anniversary Edition, Gatefold LP Jacket)',0,'Celebrating a decade of Shakey Graves'' breakout debut album, And The War Came Ten Year Anniversary Edition drops December 7, including a deluxe 2 x LP vinyl set with new gatefold art, photos, liner notes, and a personal letter from Alejandro Rose Garcia himself. The B-disc contains unearthed demos, alternate versions, and fan-favorite tracks available for the first time. The album spawned the RIAA Certified Gold single, "Dearly Departed (feat. Esme Patterson)," and helped usher in a new folk revival in 2014 as Shakey Graves performed Conan, Letterman, Seth Meyers, Austin City Limits, and Tiny Desk all in the same run leading to his Best Emerging Artist crown at the 2015 Americana Music Awards. Since then, the album has racked up over 245 million streams and sold more than 95,000 copies.','12/13/2024',1.409999999999999921,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/05/4376905-3307882.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184088,'jvc|jack van cleaf|jack van cleaf|lp','Jvc [Explicit Content]','Jack Van Cleaf','Jack Van Cleaf','LP','DUAT28581.1','803020285811',17.19000000000000127,17.19000000000000127,'44948276','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302028581','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics, Bonus Tracks)',0,'This album is all about the vertigo of growing up," says Jack, who makes his Dualtone Records debut with the sophomore release JVC. "It''s about re-defining and re-understanding yourself." "Rattlesnake," with it''s introspective lyrics and atmospheric acoustics, earned him a spot on Spotify''s 2024 Best New Artist list with tastemaker playlist "juniper." JVC was born during a period of anxiety, self-examination, and newfound freedom. It''s a sharply-written record that measures the long, winding road from past to present.','5/9/2025',1.0,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/74/4404574-3324649.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184089,'the dreamin kind|langhorne slim|langhorne slim|lp','The Dreamin'' Kind [Explicit Content]','Langhorne Slim','Langhorne Slim','LP','DUAT29141.1','803020291416',18.80000000000000071,18.80000000000000071,'45573835','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302029141','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'Leave it to Langhorne Slim - a pioneer of raw, rule-breaking Americana for more than two decades - to reach far beyond the genre he helped inspire. The Dreamin'' Kind finds the Nashville transplant strapping on an electric guitar and embracing his longtime love of larger-than-life rock & roll. With it''s chugging power chords, 1970s-sized riffs, and richly layered arrangements, The Dreamin'' Kind is fueled not only by sheer amplification, but by the soul-baring songwriting that''s become Slim''s calling card, too. Tucked between those anthems are acoustic-driven songs that skirt the outer orbits of folk music, from the bare-boned heartbreak of "Stealin'' Time" to the organic, orchestral sweep of "Dance On Thru." The result is the more explorative and expansive album of Slim''s career: a record made for rock clubs, campfires, and garages alike, produced by Greta Van Fleet''s Sam Kiszka, and anchored by a lifelong desire to break down new walls. "It felt like I was blowing some old shit up so I could plant some new flowers," Slim says of the creation process. "I love acoustic music. I love folk music. But those aren''t my only loves. Rock & roll has always tickled the same place in my soul as great singer-songwriter music, and I wanted to explore those influences. Raw songs that make you feel something: that''s the stuff I''m after."','1/16/2026',0.5500000000000000444,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/53/4462153-3513653.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184090,'automatic|the lumineers|the lumineers|lp','Automatic [Explicit Content]','The Lumineers','The Lumineers','LP','DUAT27881.1','803020278813',15.99000000000000021,15.99000000000000021,'44772680','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302027881','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'Vinyl LP pressing. Since their breakout 2012 self-titled debut album, The Lumineers have achieved some incredible milestones: twenty-four number one hits, billions of streams, packed global arena tours, multi-platinum releases, Grammy nominations, and, most important to core members Jeremiah Fraites and Wesley Schultz, numerous beloved, timeless songs. The band''s fifth studio album Automatic out February 14, is being released in a music landscape that has become dominated by solo artists dependent on other writers. Schultz says being one of the few groups touring who write all their own material, is "a unique badge of honor." But that''s not to say they won''t collaborate with other artists; Schultz and Fraites have recently written and appeared on songs with pop icon P!nk, as well as rising singer-songwriters James Bay and Zach Bryan','2/14/2025',0.7600000000000000088,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/27/4387527-3291842.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184091,'and the war came 10 year anniversary edition iex|shakey graves|shakey graves|lp','And the War Came: 10 Year Anniversary Edition (IEX)','Shakey Graves','Shakey Graves','LP','DUAT28051.1','803020280519',25.33999999999999986,25.33999999999999986,'46591234','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302028051','(Colored Vinyl, Limited Edition, Indie Exclusive, Gatefold LP Jacket, Anniversary Edition)',0,'Celebrating a decade of Shakey Graves'' breakout debut album, And The War Came Ten Year Anniversary Edition drops December 7, including a deluxe 2 x LP vinyl set with new gatefold art, photos, liner notes, and a personal letter from Alejandro Rose Garcia himself. The B-disc contains unearthed demos, alternate versions, and fan-favorite tracks available for the first time. The album spawned the RIAA Certified Gold single, Dearly Departed (feat. Esme Patterson), and helped usher in a new folk revival in 2014 as Shakey Graves performed Conan, Letterman, Seth Meyers, Austin City Limits, and Tiny Desk all in the same run leading to his Best Emerging Artist crown at the 2015 Americana Music Awards. Since then, the album has racked up over 245 million streams and sold more than 95,000 copies.','10/23/2026',1.429999999999999938,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/14/4542114-3720224.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184092,'culture of fear rsd|thievery corporation||lp','Culture of Fear (RSD)','Thievery Corporation',NULL,'LP','THVY8793.1','79275587936',21.5,NULL,NULL,'2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/thievery-corporation-culture-of-fear-rsd/79275587936',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184093,'fondness etc|shakey graves|shakey graves|lp','Fondness, Etc.','Shakey Graves','Shakey Graves','LP','DUAT30841.1','803020308411',18.80000000000000071,18.80000000000000071,'46051226','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302030841',NULL,0,'Long celebrated as one of America''s most inventive DIY singer-songwriters, Shakey Graves (born Alejandro Rose-Garcia) has built a singular career on experimentation and emotional honesty. Fondness, etc. Feels like a window into his most personal world yet - and a full creative reset - placing emphasis on lo-fi sound and analog warmth, packed with soft vocals, haunted guitars, experimental textures, and tender imperfections. His songs explore trying to do better and holding onto fleeting beauty in a chaotic world. The title is a twist on "absence makes the heart grow fonder," delivered with classic Shakey self-effacing charm - capturing moments of life, love, and fatherhood with striking vulnerability and sonic exploration. An album built purely for joy, reminding us that the quietest moments often hold the most profound beauty.','5/15/2026',0.5799999999999999601,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/33/4497133-3537234.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184094,'brightside|the lumineers|the lumineers|lp','Brightside','The Lumineers','The Lumineers','LP','DUAT2249.1','803020224919',13.68999999999999951,13.68999999999999951,'42040866','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302022491',NULL,0,'Multi-platinum selling GRAMMY-nominated band The Lumineers are back with their fourth record,  ∩╗┐BRIGHTSIDE∩╗┐, releasing January 14, 2022 on Dualtone. ∩╗┐Coming off the success of their darkly cinematic third record ∩╗┐III∩╗┐, Wesley Schultz and Jeremiah Fraites'' latest work is their most spontaneous and joyous yet, featuring their ever-more-sophisticated songwriting and arranging and production from longtime producer and friend Simone Felice. The lead single and title track "BRIGHTSIDE, " recorded in just one day, sets off the album with an anthemic bang, touching on themes of love and American life and featuring the foot-stomping, arena-filling sound the band has become beloved for worldwide. "... this time it was bare bones, " Schultz expressed. "We started demoing in Jer''s basement and didn''t even touch the computer - we just used my phone to record voice memos on, and that was what we sent to Simone. For me, it was about wanting to have more curiosity in the studio and not have everything all dialed in. It felt like a new path."','1/14/2022',0.7800000000000000266,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/41/4011641-2748105.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184095,'far out country i ii|futurebirds|futurebirds|lp','Far Out Country I&II [Explicit Content]','Futurebirds','Futurebirds','LP','DUAT30901.1','803020309012',25.33999999999999986,25.33999999999999986,'46115492','2026-11-10 23:57:36','2026-11-10 23:57:36','/80302030901','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'After more than 15 years together, Futurebirds have channeled everything they''ve lived and learned into their best project yet-one that elevates and adds new dimension to their signature cosmic Americana, psychedelic country-rock sound. Fronted by three singer-songwriters-Daniel Womack, Carter King, and Thomas Johnson-whose voices are shaped by a shared history yet distinct lives and personalities, the band teamed up with Grammy-winning producer Brad Cook (Waxahatchee, MJ Lenderman) on an album that embraces life in all it''s chaos and the evolving bonds that hold them together.','6/5/2026',0.959999999999999965,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/33/4503733-3553004.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184096,'far out country i ii|futurebirds|futurebirds|lp','Far Out Country I&II [Explicit Content]','Futurebirds','Futurebirds','LP','DUAT31251.1','803020312517',28.58999999999999986,28.58999999999999986,'46115508','2026-11-10 23:57:37','2026-11-10 23:57:37','/80302031251','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics, Colored Vinyl)',0,'After more than 15 years together, Futurebirds have channeled everything they''ve lived and learned into their best project yet-one that elevates and adds new dimension to their signature cosmic Americana, psychedelic country-rock sound. Fronted by three singer-songwriters-Daniel Womack, Carter King, and Thomas Johnson-whose voices are shaped by a shared history yet distinct lives and personalities, the band teamed up with Grammy-winning producer Brad Cook (Waxahatchee, MJ Lenderman) on an album that embraces life in all it''s chaos and the evolving bonds that hold them together.','6/5/2026',1.050000000000000044,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/34/4503734-3553005.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184097,'i think i had something once blue|aubory bugg|aubory bugg|lp','I Think I Had Something Once - Blue [Explicit Content]','Aubory Bugg','Aubory Bugg','LP','DUAT31451.1','803020314511',18.80000000000000071,18.80000000000000071,'46382276','2026-11-10 23:57:37','2026-11-10 23:57:37','/80302031451','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics, Colored Vinyl, Blue)',0,'By 13, Aubory Bugg was already turning personal experience into songs at local coffee houses - her search for belonging in a conservative, tight-knit town becoming the tension at the heart of her songwriting. Raised on Bonnie Raitt and Carole King, she found a new blueprint in independent artists like Lizzy McAlpine and Jensen McCrae, who were building careers online without compromising their artistry. When family hardship forced her to leave college, Aubory didn''t step back from music - she leaned in harder. Juggling two jobs, she committed to posting a cover every day on TikTok. Her cover of Renee Rapp''s "Tummy Hurts" went viral, introducing thousands of listeners. Now 21, Aubory''s debut album i think i had something once captures a pivotal chapter of identity, independence, and leaving home behind. From heartbreak to nostalgia to grief, the record traces the many shapes of loss - and what it takes to move through it.','9/18/2026',0.6199999999999999956,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/05/4523705-3625766.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184098,'live from orlando|flipturn|flipturn|lp','Live From Orlando [Explicit Content]','Flipturn','Flipturn','LP','DUAT29961.1','803020299610',25.33999999999999986,25.33999999999999986,'45544194','2026-11-10 23:57:37','2026-11-10 23:57:37','/80302029961','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'Flipturn''s first ever live album, recorded across two sold-out nights at the House of Blues in Orlando, FL this spring. Includes fans favorites and streaming hits like August, Chicago, Sad Disco, and more.','12/12/2025',1.09000000000000008,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/17/4459317-3452395.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184099,'i am a prism|judah the lion|judah the lion|lp','I Am a Prism','Judah & the Lion','Judah & the Lion','LP','DUAT31321.1','803020313217',18.80000000000000071,18.80000000000000071,'46279781','2026-11-10 23:57:37','2026-11-10 23:57:37','/80302031321',NULL,0,'Judah & the Lion return with I Am A Prism (August 14), their most expansive and emotionally resonant album to date. Rising from Belmont University dorm rooms to #1 Alternative hits and arena stages, the band continues to push their genre-blurring ethos forward-this time with a bold, kaleidoscopic sound that spans 80s-inflected rock ("Miracle," "Win or Go Home"), arena-ready alt-pop ("Maybe the Best Is Now"), soulful introspection ("As The Crow"), and even a tongue-in-cheek pop-country turn ("Gravel Roads"). Produced by Jeremy Lutito and mixed by Ryan Hewitt, the album captures both scale and intimacy-incorporating live audience recordings that blur the line between performance and community. At it''s core, I Am A Prism reflects the band''s deeply human journey: navigating faith, identity, relationships, and reinvention with a rare mix of vulnerability and competitive fire. It''s that tension-Beastie Boys energy meeting folk roots-that has defined their rise and continues to set them apart.','8/14/2026',0.6099999999999999867,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/58/4515658-3598310.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184100,'i am a prism|judah the lion|judah the lion|cd','I Am a Prism','Judah & the Lion','Judah & the Lion','CD','DUAT31322.2','803020313224',9.0,9.0,'46279798','2026-11-10 23:57:37','2026-11-10 23:57:37','/80302031322',NULL,0,'Judah & the Lion return with I Am A Prism (August 14), their most expansive and emotionally resonant album to date. Rising from Belmont University dorm rooms to #1 Alternative hits and arena stages, the band continues to push their genre-blurring ethos forward-this time with a bold, kaleidoscopic sound that spans 80s-inflected rock ("Miracle," "Win or Go Home"), arena-ready alt-pop ("Maybe the Best Is Now"), soulful introspection ("As The Crow"), and even a tongue-in-cheek pop-country turn ("Gravel Roads"). Produced by Jeremy Lutito and mixed by Ryan Hewitt, the album captures both scale and intimacy-incorporating live audience recordings that blur the line between performance and community. At it''s core, I Am A Prism reflects the band''s deeply human journey: navigating faith, identity, relationships, and reinvention with a rare mix of vulnerability and competitive fire. It''s that tension-Beastie Boys energy meeting folk roots-that has defined their rise and continues to set them apart.','8/14/2026',0.0100000000000000002,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/59/4515659-3598312.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184101,'hurry demo b w drifter demo orange||suicide squeeze|7 single','Hurry (Demo) B/ W Drifter (Demo) - Orange',NULL,'Suicide Squeeze','7" Single','SSQ246C1.7','803238024677',8.0,8.0,'45477553','2026-11-10 23:57:37','2026-11-10 23:57:37','/80323802467','(Colored Vinyl, Orange)',0,'Unearthed from the margins of Nosebleed Weekend, these two tracks offer a raw, revealing glimpse into The Coathangers'' creative process, capturing a band mid-stride, sorting through instinct and intention. "Hurry" and "Drifter" were both written and demoed during the sessions for that record but ultimately shelved, left to simmer in the archives. Years later, vocalist Julia Kugel returned to them with fresh ears and found something vital: a looseness, a spark. "Hurry" began as an instrument-swap experiment-Julia on drums, Stephanie on guitar-with a beat-up charm and feral momentum. It''s rhythm section is propulsive, the guitars overdriven and wiry, the vocals echoing with a kind of private urgency. It doesn''t Polish itself up, and that''s the point, it feels like a band finding something new in the act of not overthinking. "Drifter," meanwhile, features an early version of a song that later appeared on the Parasite EP, this time with a lighter step-the distortion dialed back just enough to let the vocal melody lean forward, more assured. It feels like a bit of time travel to the band''s rawest instincts. There''s an immediacy to both tracks, sketches made during the chaos of album-making, alive with experimentation and risk. Pressed to 7" by Suicide Squeeze, the tracks are less about perfection and more about process: evidence of the Coathangers'' ability to trust their guts, and let things breathe.','10/31/2025',0.1499999999999999945,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/12/4454112-3444020.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184102,'bedtime for democracy import|dead kennedys|dead kennedys|lp','Bedtime For Democracy [Import]','Dead Kennedys','Dead Kennedys','LP','IMT4153249.1','803341532496',28.12000000000000099,28.12000000000000099,'41815663','2026-11-10 23:57:37','2026-11-10 23:57:37','/80334153249','(United Kingdom - Import)',0,NULL,'7/16/2021',0.6400000000000000133,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/31/3987131-2724500.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184103,'awake|tycho|tycho|lp','Awake','Tycho','Tycho','LP','GHOS208.1','804297820873',15.5,15.5,'42222835','2026-11-10 23:57:37','2026-11-10 23:57:37','/80429782087','(Colored Vinyl, Clear Vinyl)',0,'For the first time on Clear color vinyl. For nearly a decade, Tycho (aka has been known as the musical alias of Scott Hansen, but with the release of Awake - his second LP for Ghostly International - the solo project has evolved into a three-piece band. Relating closer to post-rock than ambient soundscapes, the record is situated in the present, sounding more like Hansen than drawing from his influences. "This is, in many ways, the first true Tycho record." Previous Tycho releases came to fruition when an amalgam of songs were nearing completion, but Awake is where music becomes the focus and true expression becomes the result.','3/18/2014',0.5300000000000000266,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/99/4027299-2763557.jpg?ae=4621895153','Electronic');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184104,'dopethrone|electric wizard|electric wizard|lp','Dopethrone','Electric Wizard','Electric Wizard','LP','RABO73D.1','803341638358',34.67999999999999972,34.67999999999999972,'46363411','2026-11-10 23:57:37','2026-11-10 23:57:37','/80334163835','(Colored Vinyl, Blue)',0,'Limited Ice Blue Vinyl edition of the bands seminal 2000 album DOPETHRONE!!!Dopethrone, along with "Come My Fanatics" is often cited as Electric Wizard''s seminal release and the highpoint of their career.','7/31/2026',1.199999999999999956,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/30/4484730-3588100.jpg?ae=4621895153','Heavy Metal');
