INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184399,'metal fingers presents special herbs vol 9 10 green|mf doom|mf doom|lp','Metal Fingers Presents: Special Herbs Vol. 9 & 10 - Green','MF Doom','MF Doom','LP','MFCR368C1.1','826257038616',22.39000000000000056,22.39000000000000056,'45363412','2026-11-10 23:57:56','2026-11-10 23:57:56','/82625703861','(Colored Vinyl, Green)',0,'One of the most expansive instrumental Hip Hop series to date, MF Doom''s lauded Special Herbs collection assembles a mountainous collection of his beats, ranging from series exclusives to slightly reworked favorites he produced for himself and others. Released under the alias Metal Fingers, Special Herbs succeeds at capturing DOOM''s highly influential sound which continually breaks and reinterprets the rules of the game in favor of the super-villain. The world is a treasure trove of sounds, and the Metal-Fingered DOOM accepts no limits; ''70s Soul/Funk classic, ''80s R&B hits, rap nostalgia, and even soundbites from children''s records & TV all find their place in the ingredients needed to perfect his recipes.','9/5/2025',1.139999999999999902,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/40/4443440-3444801.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rap/Hip Hop');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184400,'operation doomsday|mf doom|mf doom|lp','Operation: Doomsday [Explicit Content]','MF Doom','MF Doom','LP','MFCR352.1','826257035219',22.39000000000000056,22.39000000000000056,'43283538','2026-11-10 23:57:56','2026-11-10 23:57:56','/82625703521','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'Underneath his mysterious metal mask, MF Doom hides the cachet underground legends are made of. After his first group KMD''s sophomore album Black Bastards was shelved by Elektra in 1994, and his blood brother Subroc - one half of the sibling rap duo - passed away, surviving frontman Zev Love X slowly mutated into the supervillain MC known as MF Doom, and the rap world is better for it. The 1999 release of Operation: Doomsday marked MF Doom''s official debut, reintroducing a mysterious figure who would soon become one of underground rap''s greatest voices. Within it''s 19 tracks, Operation: Doomsday reveals the confluence of DOOM''s tragic past, personal interests and daring creativity. His clever rhymes and remarkable schemes stood out against the landscape, and every sound he touched - from cartoon theme songs, to ''80s soul, to rap classics and more - got reinterpreted into something brand new and surreal. Decades later, MF Doom is still celebrated for all facets of his work and influence. In the face of tragedy, DOOM re-infiltrated the rap game on his own terms, and crafted an instant cult classic. Operation: Doomsday stands as a testament to the power of betting on yourself against all odds.','3/31/2023',0.8599999999999999867,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/86/4179086-3595319.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rap/Hip Hop');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184401,'mm food 20th anniversary|mf doom|mf doom|cd','Mm..Food (20th Anniversary) [Explicit Content]','MF Doom','MF Doom','CD','RYMS400.2','826257040022',9.5,9.5,'44612481','2026-11-10 23:57:56','2026-11-10 23:57:56','/82625704002','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics, Anniversary Edition)',0,'Originally released in 2004, MF Doom''s MM.FOOD is hailed as a classic hip-hop album full of inventive production, remarkable wordplay, and unique themes. Celebrated for it''s seamless blend of humor, wit, and social commentary, the album ushers listeners into a bizarre world of food-related metaphors, painting a bitterly comedic portrait of a life tainted by vice, violence, and jealousy. It was a brilliant and novel concept that gave DOOM plenty of room to explore the album''s subjects. Throughout MM.FOOD, DOOM embeds complex ideas within seemingly simple narratives. Album opener "Beef Rapp" is a multi-pronged metaphor reminding listeners of the dangers involved in the glorification of conflict, especially within the rap game. "Hoe Cakes" borrows it''s name from the sweet, hot water cornmeal patties, which he uses as a symbol to rhyme about indulgence and excess. Continuing the motif, he uses the Madlib-produced "One Beer" to fold layers of depth about escapism and ego, while the popular "Rapp Snitch Knishes" critiques the self-incrimination and contradictory behaviors of some rappers. Overall, MM.FOOD is both a social commentary and a piece of social satire, showcasing MF Doom''s ability to blend serious themes with his unique, playful lyrical style. The 20 Year Anniversary Edition of MM.. FOOD has completely new artwork by Sam Rodriguez.','11/15/2024',0.1300000000000000044,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/95/4369995-3232158.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rap/Hip Hop');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184402,'god loves ugly|atmosphere|atmosphere|lp','God Loves Ugly [Explicit Content]','Atmosphere','Atmosphere','LP','RYMS3119.1','826257003119',20.46999999999999887,20.46999999999999887,'39377463','2026-11-10 23:57:56','2026-11-10 23:57:56','/82625700311','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'Vinyl LP pressing. Atmosphere''s third official studio release, the critically-acclaimed God Loves Ugly, has been re-packaged for re-issue, but it remains as ugly as ever. Originally released in 2002, it helped to cement the duo''s foothold in the independent hip-hop scene, placing them at the forefront of the emerging subgenre of emo-rap. Slug and Ant weave tales of sorrow, frustration, and forgiveness together seamlessly over beds of melancholic melodies that swell with tension and angst amidst bone-cracking snares and taut bass lines. With some of the most beloved classics in Atmosphere''s catalog, including "F*** You Lucy," "Godlovesugly," "Lovelife," "Modern Man''s Hustle" and "Shrapnel," God Loves Ugly was effectively a lesson on processing pain without becoming a victim to it.','9/27/2019',1.310000000000000053,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/25/3712325-2480184.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rap/Hip Hop');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184403,'mm food 20th anniversary edition|mf doom|mf doom|lp','MM..Food (20th Anniversary Edition) [Explicit Content]','MF Doom','MF Doom','LP','RYMS493.1','826257049315',22.39000000000000056,22.39000000000000056,'46310644','2026-11-10 23:57:56','2026-11-10 23:57:56','/82625704931','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics, Anniversary Edition, Reissue)',0,'Originally released in 2004, MF Doom''s MM.FOOD is hailed as a classic hip-hop album full of inventive production, remarkable wordplay, and unique themes. Celebrated for it''s seamless blend of humor, wit, and social commentary, the album ushers listeners into a bizarre world of food-related metaphors, painting a bitterly comedic portrait of a life tainted by vice, violence, and jealousy. It was a brilliant and novel concept that gave DOOM plenty of room to explore the albums subjects. Throughout MM.FOOD, DOOM embeds complex ideas within seemingly simple narratives. Album opener Beef Rapp is a multi-pronged metaphor reminding listeners of the dangers involved in the glorification of conflict, especially within the rap game. Hoe Cakes borrows it''s name from the sweet, hot water cornmeal patties, which he uses as a symbol to rhyme about indulgence and excess. Continuing the motif, DOOM uses the Madlib-produced One Beer to fold layers of depth about escapism and ego, while the popular Rapp Snitch Knishes critiques the self-incrimination and contradictory behaviors of some rappers. Overall, MM.FOOD is both a social commentary and a piece of social satire, showcasing MF DOOMs ability to blend serious themes with his unique, playful lyrical style.','6/12/2026',1.260000000000000008,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/19/4517619-3608326.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rap/Hip Hop');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184404,'black hole superette|aesop rock|aesop rock|lp','Black Hole Superette [Explicit Content]','Aesop Rock','Aesop Rock','LP','RYMS411.1','826257041111',22.39000000000000056,22.39000000000000056,'45087479','2026-11-10 23:57:56','2026-11-10 23:57:56','/82625704111','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'Black Hole Superette, the latest album from Aesop Rock, delves into the invisible forces that shape our lives and psyches. It''s about the small, often overlooked moments-the everyday experiences that blur the lines between the real and the unreal, waking and sleeping. Aesop Rock''s signature gift for transforming the mundane into something dreamlike gives the album a surreal quality, leaving listeners questioning what''s truly real as they navigate it''s vivid, half-remembered imagery. Entirely self-produced, Black Hole Superette is one of Aesop Rock''s most technically accomplished works to date. The album''s intricate beats and complex structures provide the perfect backdrop for his expansive lyricism, balancing cerebral exploration with emotional depth. From the reflective ''Movie Night'' and the eccentric ''Send Help'' to the wistful ''Black Plums,'' Aes channels the spirit of a mad scientist, experimenting with sound and concept in ways that defy the ordinary. With a stellar lineup of collaborators that includes Lupe Fiasco, Armand Hammer, Hanni El Khatib, Open Mike Eagle and Homeboy Sandman, Black Hole Superette is dense and kinetic, an album that deftly navigates between complexity and instinct. It''s clear this project stands as one of Aesop Rock''s most multifaceted and ambitious works yet.','5/30/2025',1.179999999999999938,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/41/4418441-3378752.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rap/Hip Hop');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184405,'b day|beyonc|beyonc|lp','B''day','Beyonc├⌐','Beyonc├⌐','LP','SNY90920.1','827969092019',25.48000000000000042,25.48000000000000042,'11750345','2026-11-10 23:57:57','2026-11-10 23:57:57','/82796909201',NULL,0,'Original vinyl 2LP. Beyonc├⌐ shoots straight to #1 in 2006 on her second solo album "B''Day." In addition to the album sitting on top of the Billboard 200 chart, her single "Irreplaceable" climbed up to #1 on the Billboard Hot 100. Other songs to chart include "Beautiful Liar," "Get Me Bodied," "Deja Vu," "Ring the Alarm," "Upgrade U," "Kitty Kat" and "Green Light." That is 7 out of 11 songs! Bey went on to win the 2006 Grammy for Best Contemporary R&B Album. When it comes to the pulse of music fans, Beyonc├⌐ has her finger on it.','9/12/2006',1.260000000000000008,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/83/962983-3727518.jpg?ae=4621895153','Urban');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184406,'forever never cares|busty the bass|busty the bass|lp','Forever Never Cares','Busty & the Bass','Busty & the Bass','LP','ARCR213.1','827590213111',20.0,20.0,'45488603','2026-11-10 23:57:57','2026-11-10 23:57:57','/82759021311',NULL,0,NULL,'6/28/2024',0.7900000000000000355,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/50/4455150-3466266.jpg?ae=4621895153','Soul/R & B');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184407,'trouble mountain|aesop rock x blockhead|aesop rock x blockhead|lp','Trouble Mountain [Explicit Content]','Aesop Rock x Blockhead','Aesop Rock x Blockhead','LP','RYMS497.1','826257049711',22.39000000000000056,22.39000000000000056,'46586001','2026-11-10 23:57:57','2026-11-10 23:57:57','/82625704971','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'Nearly three decades after first forging one of underground hip-hop''s most enduring creative partnerships, Aesop Rock and Blockhead reunite for Trouble Mountain, a new full-length meditation on escape, survival, and the strange terrain of everyday life. Inspired by the nostalgic promise of Poconos resort commercials that blanketed New York airwaves during their childhoods, the album imagines a fictional getaway where the search for reinvention proves just as disorienting as the reality left behind. Arriving as Aesop Rock''s 13th studio album, Trouble Mountain finds his writing as inventive as ever-transforming family history, work, memory, and the absurd mechanics of modern life into vivid, deeply human reflections. Blockhead''s production is equally vital, pairing the duo''s unmistakable chemistry with lean, evolving soundscapes that feel both familiar and newly exploratory. Together, they revisit the themes that have connected their work since Labor Days: labor, alienation, and the enduring hope that there''s somewhere else we''d rather be. Rather than offering an escape, Trouble Mountain asks why we''re always searching for one-delivering one of the duo''s most imaginative and resonant collaborations to date.','11/13/2026',1.030000000000000026,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/26/4541626-3717960.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rap/Hip Hop');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184408,'all over the world best of electric light orch|electric light orchestra|electric light orchestra|cd','All Over the World: Best of Electric Light Orch','Electric Light Orchestra','Electric Light Orchestra','CD','SNY94489.2','827969448922',7.879999999999999894,7.879999999999999894,'10899182','2026-11-10 23:57:57','2026-11-10 23:57:57','/82796944892','(Remastered)',0,'ELO combined huge musical ambition with incredible pop smarts in a unique, idiosyncratic and brilliant fashion. This best of contains fifteen Top 40 hits along with fan favorites from a band whose stellar career spanned some fifteen years.','8/2/2005',0.2200000000000000011,'lb','https://media.aent-m.com/graphics/items/sdimages/b/500/6/4/6/1/741646.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184409,'we were dead before the ship even sank|modest mouse|modest mouse|lp','We Were Dead Before The Ship Even Sank','Modest Mouse','Modest Mouse','LP','EPIC686139.1','828768613917',32.0799999999999983,32.0799999999999983,'12125302','2026-11-10 23:57:57','2026-11-10 23:57:57','/82876861391',NULL,0,'Vinyl LP pressing of the 2007 album from the often amazing Modest Mouse. We Were Dead Before the Ship Even Sank is a new chapter in Modest Mouse''s career with the new infusion of Johnny Marr and the extra percussion muscle brought by Plummer and Peloso. The new album features several songs that the band played live during their 2-week-long sold-out runs in LA and NY, including the instant radio hit ''Dashboard.''','3/20/2007',1.370000000000000106,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/64/4387364.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184410,'the diary of alicia keys|alicia keys|alicia keys|lp','The Diary Of Alicia Keys','Alicia Keys','Alicia Keys','LP','JRCD55712.1','828765571210',26.69999999999999929,26.69999999999999929,'09657540','2026-11-10 23:57:57','2026-11-10 23:57:57','/82876557121',NULL,0,'(2-LP set)','12/16/2003',1.09000000000000008,'lbs','https://media.aent-m.com/graphics/items/sdimages/b/500/4/6/2/0/580264.jpg?ae=4621895153','Urban');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184411,'room on fire|the strokes|the strokes|lp','Room on Fire','The Strokes','The Strokes','LP','RCA55497.1','828765549714',16.80999999999999873,16.80999999999999873,'09608689','2026-11-10 23:57:57','2026-11-10 23:57:57','/82876554971',NULL,0,'Room on Fire is the second studio album by American indie rock band The Strokes. Released in October 2003, the album follows 2001''s Is This It and includes three singles: "12:51", "Reptilia", and "The End Has No End." Grammy-winning producer Nigel Godrich was initially in charge of production, but The Strokes felt he made the songs seem "soulless". The band went back to work with Is This It producer Gordon Raphael. The album features a slightly smoother sound than it''s predecessor. The bass guitar is less present except for several moments when it becomes the focal point of the song. The album title Room on Fire was drawn from a line in "Reptilia": "The room is on fire as she''s fixing her hair." The record received positive reviews upon release. It reached number two on the UK Albums Chart and debuted at number four in the U.S. on the Billboard 200, where it went on to sell 597,000 units by October 2006[citation needed] and was certified Gold.','10/28/2003',0.5300000000000000266,'lb','https://media.aent-m.com/graphics/items/sdimages/c/500/7/2/4/0/570427.jpg?ae=4621895153','Alternative Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184412,'speakerboxxx the love below|outkast|outkast|lp','Speakerboxxx: The Love Below [Explicit Content]','OutKast','OutKast','LP','LFC50133.1','828765013314',38.46000000000000085,38.46000000000000085,'09452657','2026-11-10 23:57:57','2026-11-10 23:57:57','/82876501331','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'Speakerboxxx: The Love Below OutKast The Album: Follow-up to the 3x Platinum Stankonia. First 2 singles, "She Lives In My Lap" and "Church". Bryan Barber will be shooting videos for "Ghetto Music," "She Lives In My Lap" and "Church". Jay-Z guests on the track "Flip Flop Rock." Rosario Dawson appears on "The Love Below." The Cover For This Album Is Designed So That The Back And Front Of The Album Can Be Seen As Separate Covers Featuring Either Member Of OutKast. (4 LP Set)','9/23/2003',1.620000000000000106,'lbs','https://media.aent-m.com/graphics/items/sdimages/a/500/1/0/0/6/566001.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rap/Hip Hop');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184413,'fillmore east 2 11 69|the grateful dead|the grateful dead|lp','Fillmore East 2-11-69','The Grateful Dead','The Grateful Dead','LP','FDAT2169.1','829421021698',112.0300000000000011,112.0300000000000011,'45759789','2026-11-10 23:57:57','2026-11-10 23:57:57','/82942102169','(Limited Edition, Audiophile, 180 Gram Vinyl, Anniversary Edition)',0,'Grateful Dead Fillmore East 2-11-69 (180 Gram Audiophile Vinyl/Limited Anniversary Edition/Tri-fold Cover) In celebration of 6 Decades of Grateful Dead, Friday Music is very pleased to announce this stunning 180 Gram Audiophile 3 LP Deluxe Set of Grateful DeadΓÇÖs ΓÇ£Fillmore East 2-11-69.ΓÇ¥ This amazing super limited edition treasure trove features tunes from these significant concerts, both early and late shows. Filled with 17 stellar vinyl performances, The Grateful DeadΓÇÖs Jerry Garcia, Bob Weir, Phil Lesh, Mickey Hart, Bill Kruetzmann, Ron McKernan and Tom Constanten truly radiate with some of their finest playing and singing ever, making this a wonderful listen and highly collectible album for years to come. As an added super rare treat, a tip of the hat to The Beatles is preserved in the audiophile domain with their fine interpretation of Hey Jude as well as a pair of masterful blues classics with King Bee and Good Morning Little School Girl. The Grateful DeadΓÇÖs Fillmore 2-11-69 album is packaged in a stunning tri-fold cover with artwork detailed beautifully, Gary LambertΓÇÖs original liner notes, and wonderful retro LP label artwork is also provided for each vinyl album. FEATURES: CELEBRATE 6 DECADES OF GRATEFUL DEAD THEIR GROUND BREAKING FILLMORE EAST 1969 PERFORMANCE!!! SUPER LIMITED EDITION 3 LP 180 GRAM AUDIOPHILE VINYL PRODUCED BY PHIL LESH AND JOHN CUTLER ΓÇô TAPE RESTORATION BY DAVID GLASSER & TAPE RESEARCH/COMPILATION BY DAVID LEMEIUX MASTERED IMPECCABLY BY JOE REAGOSO FROM THE ORIGINAL GRATEFUL DEAD RECORDINGS GRATEFUL DEAD / FILLMORE EAST 2-11-69','3/27/2026',1.75,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/58/4476958-3545273.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184414,'greatest hits|journey|journey|cd','Greatest Hits','Journey','Journey','CD','SNY685889.2','828768588925',7.730000000000000426,7.730000000000000426,'11641414','2026-11-10 23:57:57','2026-11-10 23:57:57','/82876858892','(Bonus Track, Expanded Version, Remastered, Digipack Packaging, Special Packaging)',0,'With over 14 million records sold this GREATEST HITS is now being reissued. Now contains the 1996 Grammy nominated hit "When You Love a Woman." 16 page booklet includes new liner notes, photos and memorabilia.','8/1/2006',0.2200000000000000011,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/78/34678-3254125.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184415,'hearts|america|america|lp','Hearts','America','America','LP','FDAT2852.1','829421285205',29.33999999999999986,29.33999999999999986,'45557699','2026-11-10 23:57:57','2026-11-10 23:57:57','/82942128520','(RSD Exclusive, Clear Vinyl, Red, Bonus Tracks, Anniversary Edition)',0,'The George Martin (The Beatles) produced smash America album "Hearts" netted the band several huge hit singles with "Daisy Jane" "Sister Goldenhair" and "Woman Tonight" Friday Music is very pleased to announce the 50th Anniversary of this amazing"Hearts" album now pressed on super limited Translucnet Red Vinyl and featuring two very rare tracks including the Spanish 45 version of "Sister Goldenhair"','11/27/2025',0.6500000000000000222,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/12/4460612-3454852.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
