INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184461,'somewhere at the bottom of the river between vega and altair|la dispute|la dispute|cd','Somewhere at the Bottom of the River Between Vega and Altair','La Dispute','La Dispute','CD','MHED1671.2','840526501076',9.5,9.5,'45831416','2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/84052650107',NULL,0,'La Dispute''s 2008 album now on CD, feaeturing hit song "Such Small Hands". La Dispute is an American post-hardcore band formed in Grand Rapids, Michigan in 2004. The band consists of vocalist Jordan Dreyer, guitarist Chad Sterenberg, drummer Brad Vander Lugt, bassist Adam Vass, and guitarist Corey Stroffolino. Known for their intense and emotionally charged sound, La Dispute has released five studio albums to critical acclaim, including "Somewhere at the Bottom of the River Between Vega and Altair" (2008), "Wildlife" (2011), and "Panorama" (2019). Their music often explores themes of loss, grief, and human relationships through a series of interconnected stories. La Dispute has developed a devoted fanbase and is known for their powerful, unforgettable live performances.','2/6/2026',0.1000000000000000055,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/13/4481013-3503391.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184462,'these things happen|saturdays at your place|saturdays at your place|lp','These Things Happen','Saturdays at Your Place','Saturdays at Your Place','LP','WXBO54.1','840526501090',16.73999999999999843,16.73999999999999843,'45730115','2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/84052650109','(Colored Vinyl)',0,'Iceberg Vinyl. On their second full-length album, these things happen, Saturdays at Your Place take everything that made their early material resonate-twinkly guitars, heart-on-sleeve songwriting, a distinctly Midwestern ache-and stretch it into something even more resonant. It''s a record about growing up without growing cold, and it''s also a testament to where they''re from (Kalamazoo, Michigan) both literally and musically; proof that a band with strong hometown roots can still shake the ground. These things happen isn''t an album that provides many answers. Instead, it''s a cathartic companion to survival with friends at your side, gear in the trailer, and enough hope to keep showing up. For Saturdays at Your Place, that''s enough.','2/20/2026',0.6099999999999999867,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/71/4474371-3492877.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184463,'i won t reach out to you silver grape|hot mulligan|hot mulligan|lp','I Won''t Reach Out to You - Silver Grape','Hot Mulligan','Hot Mulligan','LP','WXBO1000000.1','840526502233',14.73000000000000042,14.73000000000000042,'45918797','2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/84052650223','(Colored Vinyl, Silver, Purple, Reissue)',0,'Silver Grape Vinyl. Hot Mulligan''s 2021 EP, I Won''t Reach Out to You - a 5-song follow up to 2020''s critically-acclaimed album you''ll be fine. The EP includes fan-favorite track, "Featuring Mark Hoppus".','4/10/2026',0.6099999999999999867,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/29/4487329-3512668.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184464,'acoustic vol 1 2 copper emerald|hot mulligan|hot mulligan|lp','Acoustic Vol. 1 + 2 - Copper Emerald','Hot Mulligan','Hot Mulligan','LP','WXBO23.1','840526502240',16.73999999999999843,16.73999999999999843,'45918810','2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/84052650224','(Colored Vinyl, Reissue)',0,'Copper Emerald vinyl. New pressing of Hot Mulligan''s, Acoustics Vol. 1 + 2, featuring eight songs from throughout the band''s career, in addition to a Taking Back Sunday cover. When HOT MULLIGAN took to social media to declare themselves #1 Hot New Band, it would have been easy to write off the terminally online emo quartet''s proclamation as yet another irreverent entry into their bag of tricks. But it turns out Hot Mulligan have a way of manifesting things into existence, whether it''s name-dropping Michelle Branch and Mark Hoppus in song titles and netting responses from both (only one got the joke) or, true to their word, becoming synonymous with the newest waves of pop-punk and emo - err, post-emo, the genre Hot Mully have claimed responsibility for inventing. (Go ahead and fact-check it; they''ll wait.)','4/10/2026',0.589999999999999969,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/31/4487331-3512669.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184465,'if you wanna laugh you gotta cry sometimes archives vol 3 1972 197|robert lester folsom|robert lester folsom|lp','If You Wanna Laugh, You Gotta Cry Sometimes: Archives Vol. 3, 1972-197','Robert Lester Folsom','Robert Lester Folsom','LP','ATHY1401.1','840526502110',14.89000000000000056,14.89000000000000056,'45843747','2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/84052650211','(Colored Vinyl)',0,'If You Wanna Laugh, You Gotta Cry Sometimes: Archives Vol. 3, 1972-1975 is yet another magical discovery from Georgia-born singer-songwriter and guitarist Robert Lester Folsom''s oeuvre of soft psychedelia and rural Southern rock n'' roll, written and recorded over fifty years ago yet prophetically relevant today. Born of lost summers, new love (and the breaks that follow), and hippie bluegrass shakes, these spirited takes to 4-track tape capture Folsom''s earliest wizardry. A prismatic window into a young artist finding their artistic footing, and a testament to why Folsom''s legacy burns bright to this day. This edition arrives on Purple Reverie vinyl.','3/20/2026',0.5,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/09/4482609-3509327.jpg?ae=4621895153','Folk');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184466,'heart|jane remover|jane remover|lp','Heart [Explicit Content]','Jane Remover','Jane Remover','LP','DDAX230.1','840526504855',25.33999999999999986,25.33999999999999986,'45942297','2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/84052650485','(Parental Advisory Explicit Lyrics)',0,'2xLP Black Vinyl. Jane Remover is something of an internet legend. They are credited with playing a key role in the creation of the digicore music microgenre, an overstimulated relative of hyperpop. In fact, everything Jane Remover does has an overdose of stimuli: their songs are like the Tasmanian devil from Looney Tunes. A whirlwind of warped and excessive digital pop.','4/17/2026',0.8299999999999999601,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/85/4488885-3550250.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rap/Hip Hop');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184467,'you ll be fine|hot mulligan|hot mulligan|lp','You''Ll Be Fine','Hot Mulligan','Hot Mulligan','LP','WXBO52652.1','840526502219',17.5,17.5,'46129987','2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/84052650221','(Colored Vinyl, Reissue)',0,'Silver Teal Vinyl. Hot Mulligan''s 2020 release, including some of their most popular songs "*Equips Sunglasses*" and "BCKYRD" - Hot Mulligan is a ride-or-die testament to staying true to yourself. When the emo band formed in 2014 and cut their teeth playing house shows and naming songs by closing their eyes and typing into auto-correct on their phones, no one expected they''d be selling out thousand-cap venues, one of their scene''s most respected bands a decade later.','6/5/2026',0.5,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/38/4505138-3561867.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184468,'always cloudy|saturdays at your place|saturdays at your place|lp','Always Cloudy','Saturdays at Your Place','Saturdays at Your Place','LP','WXBO48.1','840526503681',16.10000000000000143,16.10000000000000143,'46030436','2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/84052650368','(Colored Vinyl, Clear Vinyl, Reissue)',0,'Blue and Clear A-Side/B-Side Vinyl. ''always cloudy'' by Saturdays at Your Place is the band''s fan-favorite 2023 EP, The EP features their hit #1 streaming song, "tarot cards".','5/1/2026',0.6099999999999999867,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/11/4495811-3533677.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184469,'two star the dream police iex|mk gee|mk gee|lp','Two Star & The Dream Police (IEX)','Mk.Gee','Mk.Gee','LP','RRRX384777.1','8405265063166',22.08999999999999986,22.08999999999999986,'46152671','2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/8405265063166','(Indie Exclusive, Colored Vinyl, Reissue)',0,'Black Marble Indie Exclusive. Two Star & The Dream Police is the latest album by songwriter, producer, and multi-instrumentalist Mk. Gee, released on February 9, 2024, through R&R. Two Star & the Dream Police blends ''80s pop, rock, and R&B, the record brimming with expansive, genre-defying, and loosely structured songs that evoke dreaminess and emotion. The record is nearly entirely self-produced along with Mk. Gee''s frequent collaborator Dijon. The record received widespread love from fans along with critical acclaim from major outlets such a Pitchfork, Rolling Stone, Stereogum, Billboard, NPR, Complex, and many many more.','6/26/2026',0.6099999999999999867,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/58/4507358-3563999.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184470,'laura marling live at albert hall manchester rsd|laura marling||lp','Laura Marling - Live At Albert Hall Manchester (RSD)','Laura Marling',NULL,'LP','CHYL1818.1','84040171818',25.98999999999999844,NULL,NULL,'2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/laura-marling-laura-marling-live-at-albert-hall-manchester-rsd/84040171818',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184471,'sugar|mayday parade|mayday parade|lp','Sugar','Mayday Parade','Mayday Parade','LP','MCXR1000333.1','840526506378',16.10000000000000143,16.10000000000000143,'46196286','2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/84052650637','(Black)',0,'Black Vinyl. By the time MAYDAY PARADE began work on Sugar, the closing installment of their three-part album series, they had pushed themselves further than ever before. Following Sweet (April 2025) and Sad (October 2025), the pop-rock quintet committed to a relentless cycle - write, record, tour, repeat - building a body of work that captures the full scope of their sound across nearly 30 songs. Sugar brings the trilogy to a close in powerful fashion, emphasizing both reflection and forward momentum through the driving emo pulse of first single "Blame It On The Youth," the hypnotic piano ballad "What Happens Next," the glossy melodic groove of "Two Hearts," and the nostalgic energy of "Sweet Sad Sugar" that reflects on the Tallahassee roots that shaped them. Just as importantly, the project marks the beginning of a new era defined by autonomy. Released independently, the set sees Mayday Parade taking full control of their creative output - a full-circle moment for a group that first built it''s audience by selling CDs in Warped Tour parking lots and quickly became a leading voice of the late-2008s emo wave thanks to gold and platinum singles like "Jamie All Over" and "Miserable At Best." It''s this willingness to chase something ambitious, no matter how daunting, that has defined them from the very beginning. Now, with the trilogy complete, Mayday Parade find themselves in a position few of their peers can claim: still creatively restless, still evolving and still finding new ways to win.','7/24/2026',0.5799999999999999601,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/45/4511245-3574005.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184472,'define the great line|underoath|underoath|lp','Define the Great Line','Underoath','Underoath','LP','MHED34320.1','840526507252',22.08999999999999986,22.08999999999999986,'46374202','2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/84052650725','(Colored Vinyl)',0,'Brown vinyl. Featuring fan favorites like "Writing On The Walls", "In Regards To Myself", and "You''re Ever So Inviting", Define the Great Line defied expectations when it debuted at No. 2 on the Billboard 200. It is widely regarded as one of the definitive heavy records of the early 2000s, solidifying Underoath''s legacy as one most influential bands of the genre. The heart of their sound, which delivers naked vulnerability with thrilling force and cinematic lushness, can be heard in generations of bands who''ve pursued their trail. But Underoath refuses to sit still. Walking an artistic tightrope between immersive access and isolationist otherness, Underoath owns the space between huge choruses and forward-thinking heaviness, both on record and onstage.','8/28/2026',1.010000000000000008,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/80/4522980-3621993.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184473,'i want to disappear in the usa|the story so far|the story so far|lp','I Want to Disappear in the USA','The Story So Far','The Story So Far','LP','MHED135346.1','840526507313',22.08999999999999986,22.08999999999999986,'46321336','2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/84052650731','(Colored Vinyl)',0,'Rainbow Road Colored Vinyl. The Story So Far is an American pop-punk band from Walnut Creek, California, formed in 2007. This is the third pressing of their live record recorded between shows in Boston and LA in 2025.','8/21/2026',1.010000000000000008,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/32/4518532-3691867.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184474,'somewhere in the between|streetlight manifesto|streetlight manifesto|lp','Somewhere in the Between','Streetlight Manifesto','Streetlight Manifesto','LP','PTTQ3030099.1','840526510245',17.5,17.5,'46199775','2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/84052651024','(Colored Vinyl, Reissue)',0,'Clear Vinyl. Streetlight''s third album (following the Keasbey Nights re-recording) refined and expanded on the sound of their debut, delivering a tighter, more polished collection of songs. The record opens with "We Will Fall Together," one of the band''s most beloved tracks, and maintains a relentless energy throughout it''s ten songs. Lyrically, Kalnoky continued exploring themes of cynicism, faith, and perseverance, wrapped in the band''s signature wall of horns and propulsive rhythms. It cemented Streetlight''s reputation and remains many fans'' pick for the band''s best work.','7/24/2026',0.6199999999999999956,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/67/4511567-3575715.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184475,'a pale white dot|periphery|periphery|lp','A Pale White Dot','Periphery','Periphery','LP','TDTT20.1','840526506774',25.33999999999999986,25.33999999999999986,'46156044','2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/84052650677','(Colored Vinyl)',0,'Half Black / Half Cream with Black Splatter Vinyl. Rebirth takes work. Just ask Periphery. The GRAMMY┬« Award-nominated quintet-Misha Mansoor [guitar, programming], Jake Bowen [guitar, programming], Matt Halpern [drums], Spencer Sotelo [vocals], and Mark Holcomb [guitar]-has quietly, yet diligently reshaped, recharged, and redefined itself over the course of nearly two decades as a unit. The band''s signature sound has evolved like any living and breathing organism would, gaining complexity and strength through life experience. Such progression has enabled the collective to deliver it''s most cohesive offering yet, A Pale White Dot [3 DOT RECORDS] Once again, you can expect Periphery''s trademark mind-blowing instrumentation, immersive soundscape architecture, cathartically crushing vocals, and cosmically catchy melodies, but you''ll also get emotional acuity, raw humanity, and a level of relatability that could only come from a group of brothers who have effectively gone through it all','7/10/2026',1.050000000000000044,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/11/4507711-3563227.jpg?ae=4621895153','Heavy Metal');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184476,'montgomery ricky plus 3|ricky montgomery|ricky montgomery|lp','Montgomery Ricky (Plus 3)','Ricky Montgomery','Ricky Montgomery','LP','MHED1010100.1','840526505128',16.10000000000000143,16.10000000000000143,'46100498','2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/84052650512','(Colored Vinyl)',0,'12" EP. The debut album from online sensation Ricky Montgomery, Montgomery Ricky, turns 10 on April 1st of 2026. It has racked up over 2.2 billion streams thanks to Platinum indie-pop hits "Mr. Loverman" and "Line Without a Hook," and both songs are set to hit 1 billion streams each before the end of 2026. Since blowing up on TikTok during the pandemic, Montgomery Ricky has averaged 1M streams per day. This year, Ricky is set to release Montgomery Ricky +3, an upcoming EP of previously unreleased songs from the Montgomery Ricky era of music that Ricky has revisited. This release features "Oh My My", a song that features the same second verse from "Line Without a Hook", and the cover art for the release will be sketches of the album that are previously unreleased.','5/29/2026',0.589999999999999969,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/67/4502367-3603367.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184477,'i love my computer|ninajirachi||lp','I Love My Computer','Ninajirachi',NULL,'LP','DDAX220.1','84052650123',21.57999999999999829,NULL,NULL,'2026-11-10 23:58:02','2026-11-10 23:58:02','/ninajirachi-i-love-my-computer/84052650123',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184478,'everything goes numb|streetlight manifesto|streetlight manifesto|lp','Everything Goes Numb','Streetlight Manifesto','Streetlight Manifesto','LP','PTTQ1993.1','840526510191',22.08999999999999986,22.08999999999999986,'46199744','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052651019','(Colored Vinyl, Reissue)',0,'Clear vinyl. Streetlight Manifesto''s debut full-length arrived in 2003 and immediately established the New Jersey band as a force in third-wave ska-punk. Fronted by Tomas Kalnoky, who had previously led Catch 22, the album blends furious horn arrangements with surprisingly dark, introspective lyrics about mortality and wasted youth. Tracks like "A Better Place, A Better Time" and "Point / Counterpoint" became instant fan favorites and remain setlist staples to this day. It developed a massive cult following and is widely considered one of the defining records of the genre.','7/24/2026',1.030000000000000026,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/64/4511564-3575711.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184479,'racing mount pleasant iex|racing mount pleasant|racing mount pleasant|lp','Racing Mount Pleasant (IEX)','Racing Mount Pleasant','Racing Mount Pleasant','LP','RRRX530049.1','840526507658',22.08999999999999986,22.08999999999999986,'46240361','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052650765','(Indie Exclusive, Colored Vinyl, Reissue)',0,'Apple Red Indie Retail Exclusive. Racing Mount Pleasant began as a group of friends and like-minded musicians in Ann Arbor anchored at a single creative house that various members of the band have frequented and to this day, continue to live in near the University of Michigan. After an early album and smattering of songs under the Kingfisher, including one beguiling and ambitious album released in 2022, the band reimagined themselves as Racing Mount Pleasant. Now the band are reintroducing themselves under this new moniker, with a beautiful, challenging self-titled debut album that draws on each member''s academic mastery of their instruments, but also a spirited defiance of conventional song structures, or even what a contemporary band looks or sounds like. The band supported Geese in the Fall and embarked on their own headline tour in 2026.','7/10/2026',0.979999999999999983,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/65/4512665-3588991.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184480,'why would i watch iex|hot mulligan|hot mulligan|lp','Why Would I Watch (IEX)','Hot Mulligan','Hot Mulligan','LP','WXBO095346.1','840526511037',17.5,17.5,'46258069','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052651103','(Indie Exclusive, Colored Vinyl, Reissue)',0,'Half Red / Half White Vinyl. When HOT MULLIGAN took to social media to declare themselves #1 Hot New Band, it would have been easy to write off the terminally online emo quartet''s proclamation as yet another irreverent entry into their bag of tricks. But it turns out Hot Mulligan have a way of manifesting things into existence, whether it''s name-dropping Michelle Branch and Mark Hoppus in song titles and netting responses from both (only one got the joke) or, true to their word, becoming synonymous with the newest waves of pop-punk and emo - err, post-emo, the genre Hot Mully have claimed responsibility for inventing. (Go ahead and fact-check it; they''ll wait.) Since forming in Lansing, Michigan, in 2014, the college friends - vocalist Tades Sanville, guitarists Chris Freeman and Ryan Malicsi and drummer Brandon Blakeley - have ascended from basements to buzz band on the back of two beloved albums, 2018''s Pilot and 2020''s you''ll be fine. Now, bolstered by hundreds of millions of Spotify streams, the band''s third LP, Why Would I Watch, cements their evolution as one the most versatile and profoundly moving bands in the underground.','7/24/2026',0.6300000000000000044,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/28/4513828-3592434.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184481,'the hands that thieve iex|streetlight manifesto|streetlight manifesto|lp','The Hands That Thieve (IEX)','Streetlight Manifesto','Streetlight Manifesto','LP','PTTQ237984.1','840526510351',22.08999999999999986,22.08999999999999986,'46199768','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052651035','(Indie Exclusive, Colored Vinyl, Reissue)',0,'Red Smoke Indie Retail Exclusive. After years of delays and a very public, bitter dispute with Victory Records, Streetlight finally delivered their follow-up to Somewhere in the Between in 2013. The album is the band''s most ambitious in terms of song length and arrangement complexity, with several tracks stretching well past the five-minute mark. It carries a slightly more mature, weathered tone than earlier records, reflecting the turbulent period the band had endured to get it released. Despite the troubled road to release, it was warmly received and stands as a worthy closer to what many consider the band''s classic era.','7/24/2026',0.660000000000000031,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/66/4511566-3575725.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184482,'the greatest hits of kenny loggins yesterday today tomorrow|kenny loggins||lp','The Greatest Hits of Kenny Loggins - Yesterday Today Tomorrow','Kenny Loggins',NULL,'LP','FRIM78896.1','82942178896',56.99000000000000198,NULL,NULL,'2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/kenny-loggins-the-greatest-hits-of-kenny-loggins-yesterday-today-tomorrow/82942178896',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184483,'never before seen never again found iex|arm s length|arm s length|lp','Never Before Seen, Never Again Found (IEX)','Arm''s Length','Arm''s Length','LP','WXBO97477.1','840526507665',17.5,17.5,'46150493','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052650766','(Indie Exclusive, Colored Vinyl, Reissue)',0,'Grape Purple Indie Exclusive. Emo three-piece Arm''s Length was formed in early 2019 in the small Canadian town of Belleville, Ontario when best friends Allen Steinberg and Jeremy Whyte finally began writing music together after years of knowing each other. Meeting at a Halloween party in 2015, it seemed like fate that two open-tuning slinging guitar players would ever cross paths in their tiny suburban town. Setting out to create a great new indie infused emo sound with shades of pop-punk, Arm''s Length has made huge waves in this scene with the releases of their first two EPs, What''s Mine Is Yours and Everything Nice including coverage on Pitchfork, NPR, and more.','6/26/2026',0.5799999999999999601,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/41/4507141-3562270.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184484,'it s a mystery charlie brown|vince guaraldi|vince guaraldi|lp','It''s a Mystery, Charlie Brown','Vince Guaraldi','Vince Guaraldi','LP','LMFP650975.1','840526509751',24.48999999999999844,24.48999999999999844,'46246141','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052650975','(Indie Exclusive, Clear Vinyl, Remastered, Restored)',0,'Premiere of the 12", BioVinyl LP, celebrating 75 years since Vince Guaraldi started his professional music career. There are four bonus tracks from the ΓÇ£Mystery sessionΓÇ¥ and two additional jazz standards recorded around the same time, featuring Ron McClure on bass. Mystery was the 11th Peanuts special that Guaraldi composed and performed on piano. The quartet features Seward McCain - Bass, Mike Clark/Eliot Zigmund ΓÇô drums, and Tom Harrell - trumpet. The special aired on 2-1-1974, written by Charles Schulz, produced by Bill Melendez and Lee Mendelson, and directed by Phil Roman. Available for the first time ever on Vinyl, CD, and digital. The record was mixed and mastered for audiophiles, jazz lovers, and Peanuts fans everywhere. Terry Carleton mixed "Mystery" at Bones, and Knives Studio, Vinson Hudson restored and mastered the album, and Sean & Jason Mendelson produced the record. The LP includes a 4-page insert with art from the special, liner notes by Sean & Jason Mendelson, and Derrick Bang (author of "Vince Guaraldi at the Piano"), and it comes with a magnifying glass to help solve some of the MYSTERIES in the release. The ThinkIndie exclusive record comes in a clear ΓÇ£magnifying glassΓÇ¥ BioVinyl variant. It does not magnify, but it will help with solving all the mysteries to be discovered inside.','9/11/2026',0.05999999999999999778,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/28/4512928-3686650.jpg?ae=4621895153','Jazz');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184485,'the hands that thieve|streetlight manifesto|streetlight manifesto|lp','The Hands That Thieve','Streetlight Manifesto','Streetlight Manifesto','LP','PTTQ457333.1','840526510344',22.08999999999999986,22.08999999999999986,'46199805','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052651034','(Colored Vinyl, Reissue)',0,'Clear vinyl. After years of delays and a very public, bitter dispute with Victory Records, Streetlight finally delivered their follow-up to Somewhere in the Between in 2013. The album is the band''s most ambitious in terms of song length and arrangement complexity, with several tracks stretching well past the five-minute mark. It carries a slightly more mature, weathered tone than earlier records, reflecting the turbulent period the band had endured to get it released. Despite the troubled road to release, it was warmly received and stands as a worthy closer to what many consider the band''s classic era.','7/24/2026',0.6500000000000000222,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/70/4511570-3575723.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184486,'99 songs of revolution vol 1|streetlight manifesto|streetlight manifesto|lp','99 Songs of Revolution Vol. 1','Streetlight Manifesto','Streetlight Manifesto','LP','PTTQ38884.1','840526510290',17.5,17.5,'46199799','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052651029','(Colored Vinyl, Reissue)',0,'Clear vinyl. Originally conceived as a massive multi-band, multi-volume covers project, this album saw Streetlight tackle eleven songs that influenced Kalnoky''s musical development. The tracklist is a genuinely eclectic mix, ranging from Radiohead and Bad Religion to Paul Simon and a 1950s Louis Jordan number. Rather than simple recreations, the band fully transforms each song through their own lens, making the covers feel like natural extensions of their catalog. Only one volume was ever released, leaving the larger 99-song concept permanently unfinished.','7/24/2026',0.660000000000000031,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/69/4511569-3575719.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184487,'orange blossoms iex|goldford|goldford|lp','Orange Blossoms (IEX)','Goldford','Goldford','LP','MYHX1304.1','840526511112',17.5,17.5,'46321343','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052651111','(Indie Exclusive, Colored Vinyl)',0,'"Goldford''s soul music is rooted in truth. On his breakout EP "Orange Blossoms," his raw, unvarnished songs are a balance of introspection and catharsis, grappling with heartbreak, healing, and the quiet revelations that come with growth. After spending a decade in corporate America, the St. Louis native (now based in Los Angeles) turned to music as a means of survival following a devastating personal loss. "I was more afraid of dying with regret than I was of failing," he says of his decision to finally choose the path at 30, a choice that set his entire trajectory in motion. That initial fearlessness has since fueled extraordinary momentum. Goldford has rapidly become one of the most compelling emerging voices in contemporary music.','7/31/2026',0.6300000000000000044,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/33/4518533-3606389.jpg?ae=4621895153','Folk');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184488,'daredevil|fu manchu|fu manchu|lp','Daredevil','Fu Manchu','Fu Manchu','LP','ADOJ651167.1','840526511679',23.26999999999999958,23.26999999999999958,'46248190','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052651167','(Indie Exclusive, Limited Edition, Colored Vinyl, Blue)',0,NULL,'7/31/2026',0.5799999999999999601,'lb','https://webami.aent.com/content/img/no_image_CD_lrg.gif','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184489,'mother earth s plantasia 50th anniversary edition|mort garson|mort garson|lp','Mother Earth''s Plantasia (50th Anniversary Edition)','Mort Garson','Mort Garson','LP','SBON30300.1','840526511839',18.80000000000000071,18.80000000000000071,'46382405','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052651183','(Colored Vinyl, Anniversary Edition)',0,'Before Brian Eno popularized discreet music, Juilliard-educated composer and session player Mort Garson was already crafting lush, curious sound worlds, from lounge hits and the 1969 moon-landing broadcast to arrangements for Doris Day and Glen Campbell; by the mid-1970s, as The Secret Life of Plants turned specious claims about plant consciousness, telepathy, and musical preference into a nationwide craze, houseplants filled American homes and Garson''s Mother Earth''s Plantasia arrived as the perfect soundtrack: "warm earth music for plants... and the people that love them," performed on the new-fangled Moog with bucolic, charming, stoner-friendly whimsy. Originally distributed through plant shops and even mattress purchases, the album seemed like a strange artifact of 1970s plant mania, but decades later it blossomed into a cult classic, with Sacred Bones'' 2019 reissue introducing it to a wider global audience and helping transform it into a streaming-era touchstone. Now, 50 years after it''s original release, Mother Earth''s Plantasia stands as an enduring reminder of Garson''s singular gift for making the synthetic feel strangely alive and the whimsical feel oddly profound.','9/4/2026',0.7900000000000000355,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/18/4523718-3632084.jpg?ae=4621895153','Electronic');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184490,'sirenas|allah las|allah las|lp','Sirenas','Allah-Las','Allah-Las','LP','MXSU3941.1','840526512478',14.78999999999999915,14.78999999999999915,'46329271','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052651247',NULL,0,'On Sirenas, Los Angeles quartet Allah-Las explore psychic vistas of atmospheric instrumental storytelling. The band''s sixth album coalesces around a more spontaneous soundscape shaped by freeform experimentation, intuitive vibrations, and open-ended moments of inner and outer worlding. Channeling a fluid sweep of influences, from The Durutti Column, I.A.O., and Popol Vuh''s scores for Werner Herzog to Jacques Cousteau''s expansion of The Silent World beneath the ocean''s surface, Sirenas mediates on subconscious grooves loosely imagined and deeply felt, and opens up previously unimagined pathways in the process.','8/28/2026',0.5,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/93/4519193-3609199.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184491,'in search of 30th anniversary edition red blue vinyl custom ni|fu manchu|fu manchu|lp','In Search Of - 30th Anniversary Edition - Red Blue Vinyl & Custom Ni','Fu Manchu','Fu Manchu','LP','ATDO31.1','840526511501',30.80000000000000071,30.80000000000000071,'46504463','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052651150','(Colored Vinyl, Red, Blue)',0,'To celebrate the 30th Anniversary of the band''s 3rd album and major label debut from 27 February, 1996, the band is releasing In Search Of...30th Anniversary Edition. Recorded at Grandmaster Studios in Hollywood, California by the band and Brian Jenkins (KYUSS, SCREAMING TREES), "In Search Of..." is considered a classic of the ''90s and a pillar for the "stoner rock" movement. Highlights include the lead single ''Asphalt Risin'', ''Redline'' and fan favorite ''Cyclone Launch''. This limited edition 2,000 unit run is pressed on Red Blue Vinyl & Custom Night Sky Vinyl with each LP in a printed sleeve with never before seen images and the gatefold package design includes never before seen photos of the band. The second LP contains the previously released demos for the album that the band recorded themselves in 1995 on a 4-track Tascam. Both LPs feature newly remastered audio for maximum fidelity.','10/23/2026',1.139999999999999902,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/94/4534494-3701057.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184492,'halo iex|tiffany day|tiffany day|lp','Halo (IEX)','Tiffany Day','Tiffany Day','LP','MHED387569.1','840526512959',22.08999999999999986,22.08999999999999986,'46476906','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052651295','(Indie Exclusive, Colored Vinyl)',0,'Peppermint Candy Indie Retail Exclusive Vinyl. "Tiffany Day has quickly emerged as one of the most compelling voices in hyper-digital pop, blending emotional chaos, internet-born edge, and forward-thinking production into a sound entirely her own. Born in Toronto and raised in Kansas, Tiffany first broke through with a viral cover of "Hallelujah, " building a YouTube audience of over 500, 000 subscribers before graduating high school. She began releasing original music in college, quickly developing a devoted fanbase drawn to her wit, vulnerability, and genre-fluid instincts. Her momentum culminates in her album HALO, released April 3, 2026 via Broke Records. The project debuted at #1 on the Apple Music Electronic chart and #25 on the Billboard Electronic/Dance Albums Chart, drawing early co-signs from artists like Laufey and Yunjin (LE SSERAFIM) alongside coverage from Pitchfork, The FADER, NYLON, LA Times, and more. To mark the release, Tiffany staged three headline shows - each of which sold out in under five minutes. With her production across nearly every track, HALO marks Tiffany''s most cohesive and ambitious work to date, solidifying her not just as an artist to watch, but as a defining voice in the next era of hyperpop."','10/23/2026',0.7299999999999999823,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/33/4532033-3680362.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184493,'you ll be fine iex|hot mulligan|hot mulligan|lp','You''ll Be Fine (IEX)','Hot Mulligan','Hot Mulligan','LP','WXBO45756.1','840526512768',17.5,17.5,'46375056','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052651276','(Indie Exclusive, Colored Vinyl, Reissue)',0,'Lavender Indie Retail Exclusive Vinyl. Hot Mulligan is a ride-or-die testament to staying true to yourself. When the emo band formed in 2014 and cut their teeth playing house shows and naming songs by closing their eyes and typing into auto-correct on their phones, no one expected they''d be selling out thousand-cap venues, one of their scene''s most respected bands a decade later.','9/18/2026',0.75,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/12/4523112-3714100.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184494,'acoustic vol 1 2 iex|hot mulligan|hot mulligan|lp','Acoustic Vol. 1 + 2 (IEX)','Hot Mulligan','Hot Mulligan','LP','WXBO7457.1','840526512775',16.73999999999999843,16.73999999999999843,'46375063','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052651277','(Indie Exclusive, Colored Vinyl, Reissue)',0,'Emerald Green Indie Exclusive Vinyl. Hot Mulligan is a ride-or-die testament to staying true to yourself. When the emo band formed in 2014 and cut their teeth playing house shows and naming songs by closing their eyes and typing into auto-correct on their phones, no one expected they''d be selling out thousand-cap venues, one of their scene''s most respected bands a decade later.','9/18/2026',0.589999999999999969,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/13/4523113-3623672.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184495,'dreams of summertime|goldford|goldford|lp','Dreams of Summertime','Goldford','Goldford','LP','MHED3GF.1','840526513338',22.08999999999999986,22.08999999999999986,'46534095','2026-11-10 23:58:03','2026-11-10 23:58:03','/84052651333','(Colored Vinyl)',0,'Clear with Burgundy, Orange, and Pink Splatter. Goldford''s soul music is rooted in truth. His raw, unvarnished songs are a balance of introspection and catharsis, grappling with heartbreak, healing, and the quiet revelations that come with growth. After spending a decade in corporate America, the St. Louis native (now based in Los Angeles) turned to music as a means of survival following a devastating personal loss. "I was more afraid of dying with regret than I was of failing," he says of his decision to finally choose the path at 30, a choice that set his entire trajectory in motion. That initial fearlessness has since fueled extraordinary momentum. With over 4 million monthly listeners on Spotify, Goldford has rapidly become one of the most compelling emerging voices in contemporary music. His breakout EP, Orange Blossoms (Oct 2024), has surpassed 100M streams, and his latest project, Space of the Heart (Sept 2025), has already generated 90.8M streams, 2.7M saves, and over 153,000 pieces of user-generated content across TikTok and Instagram. The standout track "Easy Does It" has reached 43.5M streams and continues to accelerate with more than 250K new weekly discoveries on Spotify. Goldford''s touring trajectory has followed the music''s rapid ascent. He began in intimate rooms like Los Angeles'' Moroccan Lounge and New York''s Baby''s All Right before embarking on a debut North American tour that sold over 25,000 tickets. This momentum carried over to his first UK and European run, which required multiple venue upgrades in cities like London and Manchester. The international momentum continued with an Australian debut in March 2026, alongside key festival appearances at Austin City Limits and Noah Kahan''s Out of the Blue. He is currently headlining 1,000+ capacity venues on the Space of the Heart North American tour, including sold out shows in historic rooms like The Fonda and Webster Hall, with upcoming festival slots at Shaky Knees and Oceans Calling.','11/13/2026',0.5699999999999999512,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/20/4536920-3696760.jpg?ae=4621895153','Folk');
