INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184547,'the sound a body makes when it s still sea blue|hot mulligan|hot mulligan|lp','The Sound a Body Makes When It''s Still - Sea Blue','Hot Mulligan','Hot Mulligan','LP','WXGQ50.1','843563190401',16.98000000000000042,16.98000000000000042,'45204081','2026-11-10 23:58:06','2026-11-10 23:58:06','/84356319040','(Colored Vinyl, Blue)',0,'Sea Blue Vinyl. Hot Mulligan is a ride-or-die testament to staying true to yourself. When the emo band formed in 2014 and cut their teeth playing house shows and naming songs by closing their eyes and typing into auto-correct on their phones, no one expected they''d be selling out thousand-cap venues, one of their scene''s most respected bands a decade later. But as Hot Mully releases their phenomenal fourth LP, The Sound a Body Makes When It''s Still, that''s exactly where they''re at. Hot Mulligan is a resounding success story, the #1 Hot New Band (11 years running, just ask them), and ready to keep fighting the good fight. A sense of fear lives and breathes throughout the album, in blistering choruses alongside the most vulnerable moments Hot Mulligan has ever laid to tape. That being said, this is still a Hot Mulligan record, and that means it rocks. Through it all, Hot Mulligan and longtime producer Brett Romnes laid down a masterclass. The Sound a Body Makes When It''s Still grabs your attention with all it''s fight-or-flight hooks, but it''s the little nuances and connective tissue that make it Hot Mulligan''s most cohesive album yet.','8/22/2025',0.7199999999999999734,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/03/4428603-3404596.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184548,'everything nice what s mine is yours|arm s length|arm s length|lp','Everything Nice /  What''s Mine Is Yours','Arm''s Length','Arm''s Length','LP','WXBO11.1','843563188767',16.10000000000000143,16.10000000000000143,'45122859','2026-11-10 23:58:06','2026-11-10 23:58:06','/84356318876','(Colored Vinyl)',0,'Onyx Vinyl, new 2025 pressing. Arm''s Length was formed in early 2019 in the small Canadian town of Belleville, Ontario when best friends Allen Steinberg and Jeremy Whyte finally began writing music together after years of knowing each other. Setting out to create a great new indie infused emo sound with shades of pop-punk, Arm''s Length made waves in this scene with the release of their first two EPs, What''s Mine Is Yours and Everything Nice in 2019 and 2021 respectively, including coverage on Pitchfork, NPR, and more. They have since released their debut album, Never Before Seen, Never Again Found in 2022, and are releasing a new album in 2025.','6/20/2025',0.589999999999999969,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/55/4421555-3383302.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(184549,'the sound a body makes when it s still iex apple red|hot mulligan|hot mulligan|lp','The Sound a Body Makes when It''s Still (IEX) - Apple Red','Hot Mulligan','Hot Mulligan','LP','WXGQ50IEX.1','843563190395',16.98000000000000042,16.98000000000000042,'45204104','2026-11-10 23:58:06','2026-11-10 23:58:06','/84356319039','(Indie Exclusive, Colored Vinyl, Red)',0,'Apple Red Vinyl, Indie Store Exclusive. Hot Mulligan is a ride-or-die testament to staying true to yourself. When the emo band formed in 2014 and cut their teeth playing house shows and naming songs by closing their eyes and typing into auto-correct on their phones, no one expected they''d be selling out thousand-cap venues, one of their scene''s most respected bands a decade later. But as Hot Mully releases their phenomenal fourth LP, The Sound a Body Makes When It''s Still, that''s exactly where they''re at. Hot Mulligan is a resounding success story, the #1 Hot New Band (11 years running, just ask them), and ready to keep fighting the good fight. A sense of fear lives and breathes throughout the album, in blistering choruses alongside the most vulnerable moments Hot Mulligan has ever laid to tape. That being said, this is still a Hot Mulligan record, and that means it rocks. Through it all, Hot Mulligan and longtime producer Brett Romnes laid down a masterclass. The Sound a Body Makes When It''s Still grabs your attention with all it''s fight-or-flight hooks, but it''s the little nuances and connective tissue that make it Hot Mulligan''s most cohesive album yet.','8/22/2025',0.7199999999999999734,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/05/4428605-3404595.jpg?ae=4621895153','Rock');
