INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(185486,'halfway home green|gareth|gareth|lp','Halfway Home - Green','Gareth','Gareth','LP','WOFF3375312.1','823375312802',18.0,18.0,'46517609','2026-11-21 16:08:47','2026-11-21 16:08:47','/82337531280','(Colored Vinyl, Green)',0,'Gareth''s upcoming album, Halfway Home, explores transition, belonging, and what it means to find home while building a life far from where you started. Highlights include "1,000 Lifetimes," "Changing My Mind," and the anthemic "One That Got Away." Through heartfelt storytelling and contemporary country production, the project captures Gareth''s evolution while establishing him as a distinctive international voice in country music. Green LP with printed inner sleeve','12/4/2026',0.5300000000000000266,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/84/4535784-3704774.jpg?ae=4662083153','Country');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(185487,'the preacher in paris live at the elysee montmartre rsd|bobby womack|bobby womack|lp','The Preacher in Paris - Live at the Elysee Montmartre (RSD)','Bobby Womack','Bobby Womack','LP','EMMQ5990569.1','8435395505526',30.98000000000000042,30.98000000000000042,'46514707','2026-11-21 16:08:47','2026-11-21 16:08:47','/843539550552','(RSD Exclusive)',0,'Bobby Womack was one of the most distinctive voices in soul music-singer, songwriter, and guitarist whose work bridged gospel, R&B, and funk. From his early days with The Valentinos to his classic solo recordings for United Artists Records, Womack shaped the sound of modern soul with raw emotion and fearless creativity. His songs have influenced generations of artists across soul, rock, and hip-hop. Recorded in Paris on March 15, 1976, Live at the Élysée Montmartre captures Womack at the height of his powers, delivering the intensity and charisma that made him a legendary stage performer. A powerful, previously unheard document of one of soul music''s most enduring and influential artists. Transferred from the original tape reels preserved at INA, this limited-edition 180-gram 2-LP set includes an extensive insert featuring rare photographs and specially prepared liner notes.','11/26/2026',1.209999999999999965,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/90/4535490-3702228.jpg?ae=4662083153','Jazz');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(185488,'i love my computer|ninajirachi|ninajirachi|cd','I Love My Computer','Ninajirachi','Ninajirachi','CD','MHED022.2','604675224350',9.5,9.5,'46585004','2026-11-21 16:08:47','2026-11-21 16:08:47','/60467522435',NULL,0,'CD. Nina Wilson, better known as Ninajirachi, is an Australian electronic producer who released her debut album I Love My Computer is a concept record built on her connection with her PC, swiping between genres of EDM, tech-house, speed garage, dubstep, and hyperpop. Wilson builds on the legacy of early-2000s and 2010s Australian electronic artists like PNAU and Flume using technology as a medium, a motif, and a mirror for reflection. Between remixing Princess Nokia, Deadmau5 & The Neptunes, releasing on Nina Las Vegas'' NLV Records and RL Grime''s Sable Valley, Ninajirachi has performed at Lollapalooza, EDC, Laneway, Listen Out, Splendour, Falls Festival, and more and toured with Mallrat, Charli XCX, Porter Robinson and Cashmere Cat.','11/13/2026',0.1499999999999999945,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/76/4484876-3710116.jpg?ae=4662083153','Electronic');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(185489,'your mother your mother your mother original soundtrack|son lux|son lux|lp','Your Mother Your Mother Your Mother (Original Soundtrack)','Son Lux','Son Lux','LP','WXWQ249.1','850078789860',23.5,23.5,'46724090','2026-11-21 16:08:47','2026-11-21 16:08:47','/85007878986','(Colored Vinyl, Red, White)',0,'Waxwork Records presents Your Mother Your Mother Your Mother Original Motion Picture Score by Son Lux pressed to deluxe Blood Red and Milk White swirled vinyl with red splatter, housed in heavyweight gatefold jackets with matte satin coating, and a full color printed inner sleeve. For Your Mother Your Mother Your Mother, Son Lux - Rafiq Bhatia, Ian Chang, and Ryan Lott - craft an immersive, otherworldly soundscape of yearning vocals, pummeling electronic rhythms, and digitally stretched sonics. Balancing intimacy with visceral power, the score evokes the film''s themes of parenthood, grief, love, and divinity through a boldly experimental musical language. Deluxe Blood Red and Milk White swirled vinyl with red splatter, housed in heavyweight gatefold jackets with matte satin coating, and a full color printed inner sleeve','1/15/2027',0.5,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/88/4554088-3750326.jpg?ae=4662083153','Soundtrack');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(185490,'first impressions live in paris|ahmad jamal|ahmad jamal|lp','First Impressions - Live in Paris','Ahmad Jamal','Ahmad Jamal','LP','EMMQ5990567.1','8435395505489',23.5,23.5,'46560339','2026-11-21 16:08:47','2026-11-21 16:08:47','/843539550548',NULL,0,'Few pianists in jazz have wielded space and silence as deliberately - or as devastatingly - as Ahmad Jamal. By 1971, his reputation was already formidable: Miles Davis had stated in his autobiography that "all my inspiration comes from Jamal, " his 1958 recordings at the Pershing Lounge had become some of the best-selling jazz albums of the era, and his command of the trio format was without peer. First Impressions captures him on June 25, 1971, at Studio 104 at the Maison de la Radio in Paris - home of the Orchestre Nationale de France - in a performance recorded for the ORTF and preserved in the INA archive for over five decades before finally seeing official release','10/30/2026',1.120000000000000107,'lbs','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/10/4539210-3704182.jpg?ae=4662083153','Jazz');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(185491,'lady sings the blues import|billie holiday|billie holiday|lp','Lady Sings the Blues [Import]','Billie Holiday','Billie Holiday','LP','JZWX2869680.1','8436028696802',16.48000000000000042,16.48000000000000042,'14991417','2026-11-21 16:08:47','2026-11-21 16:08:47','/843602869680',NULL,0,'High-definition premium 180gm vinyl pressing of this classic Jazz album. Jazz Wax Records. 2010.','4/6/2010',0.5799999999999999601,'lb','https://media.aent-m.com/graphics/items/sdimages/a/500/3/3/9/5/1635933.jpg?ae=4662083153','Jazz Vocals');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(185492,'pure simple 10 year anniversary edition|dolly parton|dolly parton|cd','Pure & Simple (10 Year Anniversary Edition)','Dolly Parton','Dolly Parton','CD','DQLY925.2','823375383406',9.5,9.5,'46588234','2026-11-21 16:08:48','2026-11-21 16:08:48','/82337538340','(Anniversary Edition)',0,'First released August 2016, "Pure & Simple" marked Dolly Parton''s stripped-down return to her roots, her seventh #1 country album and first chart-topper in 25 years. Born from intimate 2015 shows at the Ryman and Dollywood, Dolly and quartet captured that same raw intimacy in studio. The title track sets the tone, along with the tender "Forever Love," written for her 50th anniversary. 10 years on, revisit Dolly at her purest with this limited-edition CD reissue.','12/11/2026',0.2000000000000000111,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/01/4541801-3712797.jpg?ae=4662083153','Country');
INSERT INTO webami_products VALUES(185493,'roses|widowspeak|widowspeak|lp','Roses','Widowspeak','Widowspeak','LP','CPTK391.1','817949039110',17.0,17.0,'46712684','2026-11-21 16:08:48','2026-11-21 16:08:48','/81794903911',NULL,0,'An album called ''Roses'' would be concerned with romantic gestures. Across the ten tracks that make up the seventh and newest Widowspeak record, intimate spaces and stages of love are captured with a nostalgic, vaseline-coated lens. Candles burn inside red glass as lovers get close in a leather booth. Celebrity headshots gaze down like angels in a restaurant. Elsewhere, carnations are pressed in a black book and dancers pull each other close. Widowspeak is a band that riffs on big emotions without being too self-serious. The sweetness, even silliness, of an extended limerent phase that becomes as all-consuming as a pulpy trade paperback. Cars and their drivers serve as a way to talk about codependency. And old love gets worn in, soft as an old t-shirt. If music can simultaneously be naturalistic and noir, saturated and lush, that is Widowspeak. They''re a band that knows how to set a scene. These songs use intimate moments to talk about deeper heartaches: the restlessness inherent in modern existence, waiting around for something to happen. Or, feeling at odds with playing a role in your own life. ''Roses'' might be the most romantic Widowspeak record, but it''s also the most deeply realist: the stage is set not with dramatic overtures but the backdrop of the minutiae and repetition of daily acts. Small observations before, during, and after work: the ritual of pouring water for customers, catching a cold on your day off. Daydreaming about winning the lottery, or maybe realizing you already won. Here, love is a way to talk about what drives us, and Widowspeak suggest it can be the whole point. The light that illuminates the dark corners of a day, a life. A reason to keep going despite the pain it can cause. As the title track goes: Not all thorns will prick you, you still feel the first. And now you don''t grow roses because the one still hurts I want to be the one. Widowspeak are one of the most prolific and hardworking bands going, bubbling just under the surface. Molly Hamilton and Robert Earl Thomas are the core of the group and it''s songwriters, and they have honed their sound across sixteen years and an impressively consistent catalog. A lot has happened in that time: for them, for everyone. One of many bands to crop up in a fertile New York City music scene, they started out shuffling gear between venues now-since shuttered (Glasslands, Cake Shop, 285 Kent, Death By Audio to name a few) and their practice space in Monster Island Basement (now a Trader Joe''s). The highs and lows of a long career mean chaotic stints as road dogs traipsing across North America, fly-in gigs to Sao Paulo or Guadalajara, wrapping seven-week European tours And then down-time of years in between, considering the power of slowly building a body of work. Widowspeak is now a married couple, working day jobs in their own off-season. Robert is a carpenter, Molly a waitress. Maybe time has given Widowspeak the ability to grow slowly; ''Roses'' is unpruned and more beautiful for it; left a little wild as it stretches it''s new growth in all directions. From the opening chords of ''The Hook'' you can hear how far they''ve come: the road is open, the sky clears. The band feels at ease, and taking their time. They recorded the album last January at the Old Carpet Factory on the Greek island Hydra: a studio in an old house tucked into the village''s steep hills. It''s quiet there in winter, when the tourists have all gone home. Longtime touring members Willy Muse, John Andrews, and Noah Bond serve here as the players. ''Roses'' was then taken home and slowly, lightly tinkered with, before being deftly mixed by Alex Farrar at Drop of Sun Studios, and mastered by Greg Obis at Chicago Mastering. ''Roses'' is Widowspeak at it''s best, drawing on forever influences. There''s dream and power pop, a little Stones, maybe some Petty, open and languid ballads with the twang of a Lynchian roadhouse band Perhaps you hear REM, Yo La Tengo or Cat Power. A little Neil Young in Hamilton','12/4/2026',0.5500000000000000444,'lb','https://mediacdn.aent-m.com/prod-img/500/08/4553108-3747354.jpg?ae=4662083153','Rock');
